{"jobs":[{"id":"d3a31de0-d36c-4454-89e5-942794c67112","title":"Board Certified Behavior Analyst (BCBA)","department":"Clinical","team":"Board Certified Behavior Analysts","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"Boston","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-01-22T23:54:36.778+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":false,"workplaceType":"OnSite","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"Massachusetts","addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"Boston"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/annaautismcare/d3a31de0-d36c-4454-89e5-942794c67112","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/annaautismcare/d3a31de0-d36c-4454-89e5-942794c67112/application","descriptionHtml":"<p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Board Certified Behavior Analyst (BCBA) — ABA Therapy</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>$85,000–$115,000/yr + Monthly Bonuses | Full-Time, 40 hrs/wk | Monday–Friday | No Evenings, Weekends, or Travel</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">ANNA Autism Care is seeking an experienced, mission-driven Board Certified Behavior Analyst (BCBA) to join our clinician-led team. We specialize in early intervention ABA therapy for Autistic children under age 6, using the neuroaffirming model, Naturalistic Developmental Behavioral Intervention, or NDBI (ESDM, PRT, JASPER).</p><h2><br /><strong>Why Join ANNA?</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em><strong>Competitive Salary &amp; Monthly Bonuses: </strong></em>$85K–$115K base salary plus $30/hr for every billable hour over 100/month. Comprehensive health, dental, and vision insurance and 401(k) with company match.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em><strong>Work-Life Balance:</strong> </em>40-hour schedule, Monday–Friday. No travel, no evenings, no weekends.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em><strong>Manageable Caseloads:</strong> </em>Small, intentional caseloads so you can deliver high-quality clinical care — not just high volume, that adhere to evidence-based autism clinical care and genuine clinical growth.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em><strong>Clinician-Led, Mission-Driven Culture: </strong></em>Every decision starts with what's best for the child. We stay current with research and hold ourselves to a high clinical standard with our NDBI approach.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em><strong>Strong Team Support:</strong> </em>Regular individual and group supervision from experienced clinicians invested in your success.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em><strong>Professional Development: </strong></em>Annual CEU stipend, conference support, and clear pathways into clinical leadership.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em><strong>Purpose-Built Technology:</strong> </em>Streamlined data collection and clinical management tools so you stay focused on clients, not paperwork.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em><strong>Team Culture: </strong></em>Quarterly outings, milestone celebrations, and a team that genuinely collaborates and enjoys working together.</p><h2><br /><strong>Key Responsibilities:</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em><strong>Assessment &amp; Treatment Planning: </strong></em>Conduct comprehensive assessments and develop individualized, play-based treatment plans grounded in NDBI strategies for children ages 18 months to 6 years.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em><strong>Supervise &amp; Mentor: </strong></em>Lead and mentor a team of 5 - 6 Behavior Therapists through weekly individual and group supervision, building confident and skilled practitioners.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em><strong>Family Partnership: </strong></em>Implement a structured, curriculum-based parent training model which helps families learn NDBI strategies to practice and use at home.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em><strong>Data-Driven Decision Making: </strong></em>Monitor client progress through ongoing data collection and analysis, adjusting treatment plans proactively to drive meaningful milestones.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em><strong>Collaborative Care: </strong></em>Work closely with fellow BCBAs and report to a Clinical Director who is invested in both your growth and the quality of care delivered.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em><strong>Clinical Growth: </strong></em>Contribute to a culture of continuous learning by integrating current research and best practices in Autism and ABA therapy.</p><h2><br /><strong>Qualifications:</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em> <strong>BCBA certification (required).</strong></em></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience delivering ABA therapy to young, Autistic children, preferably under age 6.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">NDBI experience preferred (ESDM, PRT, and/or JASPER).</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Commitment to neurodiversity-affirming, evidence-based practice.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong interpersonal skills; ability to work both independently and collaboratively.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Compensation &amp; Benefits:</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Base salary: $85,000–$115,000/year</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Monthly bonus: $30/hr for every billable hour over 100/month</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Health, dental, and vision insurance</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">401(k) with company match</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Paid time off (vacation, sick, and holidays)</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Annual CEU stipend and professional development support</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Apply today and join ANNA Autism Care's mission to modernize early intervention ABA care to a higher standard.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">ANNA is an equal opportunity employer. We're committed to creating a diverse, inclusive, and supportive workplace. All qualified applicants receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, national origin, age, disability, religion, sex (including pregnancy, sexual orientation, and gender identity), or any other characteristic protected by law. If you're passionate about our mission but don't meet every qualification listed, we still encourage you to apply. Your unique perspective might be exactly what we need.\"</p>","descriptionPlain":"Board Certified Behavior Analyst (BCBA) — ABA Therapy\n\n$85,000–$115,000/yr + Monthly Bonuses | Full-Time, 40 hrs/wk | Monday–Friday | No Evenings, Weekends, or Travel\n\nANNA Autism Care is seeking an experienced, mission-driven Board Certified Behavior Analyst (BCBA) to join our clinician-led team. We specialize in early intervention ABA therapy for Autistic children under age 6, using the neuroaffirming model, Naturalistic Developmental Behavioral Intervention, or NDBI (ESDM, PRT, JASPER).\n\n\n\nWHY JOIN ANNA?\n\nCompetitive Salary & Monthly Bonuses: $85K–$115K base salary plus $30/hr for every billable hour over 100/month. Comprehensive health, dental, and vision insurance and 401(k) with company match.\n\nWork-Life Balance: 40-hour schedule, Monday–Friday. No travel, no evenings, no weekends.\n\nManageable Caseloads: Small, intentional caseloads so you can deliver high-quality clinical care — not just high volume, that adhere to evidence-based autism clinical care and genuine clinical growth.\n\nClinician-Led, Mission-Driven Culture: Every decision starts with what's best for the child. We stay current with research and hold ourselves to a high clinical standard with our NDBI approach.\n\nStrong Team Support: Regular individual and group supervision from experienced clinicians invested in your success.\n\nProfessional Development: Annual CEU stipend, conference support, and clear pathways into clinical leadership.\n\nPurpose-Built Technology: Streamlined data collection and clinical management tools so you stay focused on clients, not paperwork.\n\nTeam Culture: Quarterly outings, milestone celebrations, and a team that genuinely collaborates and enjoys working together.\n\n\n\nKEY RESPONSIBILITIES:\n\nAssessment & Treatment Planning: Conduct comprehensive assessments and develop individualized, play-based treatment plans grounded in NDBI strategies for children ages 18 months to 6 years.\n\nSupervise & Mentor: Lead and mentor a team of 5 - 6 Behavior Therapists through weekly individual and group supervision, building confident and skilled practitioners.\n\nFamily Partnership: Implement a structured, curriculum-based parent training model which helps families learn NDBI strategies to practice and use at home.\n\nData-Driven Decision Making: Monitor client progress through ongoing data collection and analysis, adjusting treatment plans proactively to drive meaningful milestones.\n\nCollaborative Care: Work closely with fellow BCBAs and report to a Clinical Director who is invested in both your growth and the quality of care delivered.\n\nClinical Growth: Contribute to a culture of continuous learning by integrating current research and best practices in Autism and ABA therapy.\n\n\n\nQUALIFICATIONS:\n\n BCBA certification (required).\n\n - Experience delivering ABA therapy to young, Autistic children, preferably under age 6.\n\n - NDBI experience preferred (ESDM, PRT, and/or JASPER).\n\n - Commitment to neurodiversity-affirming, evidence-based practice.\n\n - Strong interpersonal skills; ability to work both independently and collaboratively.\n\nCompensation & Benefits:\n\n - Base salary: $85,000–$115,000/year\n\n - Monthly bonus: $30/hr for every billable hour over 100/month\n\n - Health, dental, and vision insurance\n\n - 401(k) with company match\n\n - Paid time off (vacation, sick, and holidays)\n\n - Annual CEU stipend and professional development support\n\nApply today and join ANNA Autism Care's mission to modernize early intervention ABA care to a higher standard.\n\n\n\nANNA is an equal opportunity employer. We're committed to creating a diverse, inclusive, and supportive workplace. All qualified applicants receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, national origin, age, disability, religion, sex (including pregnancy, sexual orientation, and gender identity), or any other characteristic protected by law. If you're passionate about our mission but don't meet every qualification listed, we still encourage you to apply. Your unique perspective might be exactly what we need.\"","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"86e905e4-0e3e-4856-96fe-23147ea5c8dd","title":"Behavior Therapist ","department":"Clinical","team":"Behavior Therapists","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"Wayland","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":true,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-06-03T16:44:08.194+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":false,"workplaceType":"OnSite","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"Massachusetts","addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"Wayland"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/annaautismcare/86e905e4-0e3e-4856-96fe-23147ea5c8dd","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/annaautismcare/86e905e4-0e3e-4856-96fe-23147ea5c8dd/application","descriptionHtml":"<p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Behavior Therapist (BT) — ABA Therapy</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Starting at $24–$26/hr | Full-Time | Monday–Friday, 8:00 AM–4:30 PM | No Evenings or Weekends</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">ANNA Autism Care is hiring passionate Behavior Therapists (BTs) to deliver evidence-based, 1-on-1 therapy to children with Autism using the Naturalistic Developmental Behavioral Intervention (NDBI) approach. Registered Behavior Technician (RBT) certification is a condition of employment for this role — and ANNA makes it easy: we provide the required RBT training and cover the cost of certification at no expense to you, with paid training time and extensive clinical supervision at our center-based Autism care centers across Massachusetts. </p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>What ANNA Autism Care Offers:</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Competitive Pay + Retention Bonus</em>: $24–$26/hr starting pay, plus a $400 retention bonus after 6 months of employment.</p></li></ul><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Comprehensive Benefits:</em> Health, dental, and vision insurance, 401(k) with company matching, and paid time off.</p></li></ul><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Consistent Schedule:</em> Monday–Friday, 8:00 AM–4:30 PM. No evenings, no weekends.</p></li></ul><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Full-Time Hours: </em>25–35 hours per week with a stable clinic-based schedule working with 5–7 clients in a clinical pod.</p></li></ul><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Free RBT Certification:</em> ANNA provides the RBT 40-hour training, supervised competency assessment, and first certification exam attempt at no cost to you — with paid training time and a certification bonus for completing your RBT training within 2 weeks of starting.</p></li></ul><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">P<em>aid Training &amp; Weekly Supervision:</em> Extensive paid onboarding plus weekly clinical supervision and ongoing mentorship from BCBAs.</p></li></ul><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Career Advancement: </em>Clear promotion paths for BTs at every stage, including BCBA sponsorship for top performers (Master's in ABA tuition covered by ANNA).</p></li></ul><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Supportive Team Culture: </em>Monthly team lunches, seasonal celebrations, summer events, and a community that grows together.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Key Responsibilities:</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Implement individualized ABA therapy plans under BCBA supervision to teach new skills in communication and socialization while reducing any challenging, injurious behaviors.</p></li></ul><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Deliver play-based, child-centered therapy using the NDBI framework.</p></li></ul><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Collect accurate session data to measure each client's progress toward treatment plan goals, and communicate progress with clinical supervisors.</p></li></ul><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Assist BCBAs with assessment procedures (e.g., preference assessments and skill or behavior assessments) as directed.</p></li></ul><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Comply with applicable supervision standards, including participating in scheduled BCBA supervision and completing all required supervision and session documentation.</p></li></ul><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Obtain and maintain active Registered Behavior Technician (RBT) certification in good standing, including BACB supervision, renewal, and ethics requirements.</p></li></ul><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Build positive relationships with children and families, providing caregivers with daily updates.</p></li></ul><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Maintain a safe, organized and engaging therapy environment.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Qualifications:</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Registered Behavior Technician (RBT) certification — required as a condition of employment. </strong>Candidates who are not yet certified must complete ANNA's paid RBT training program (40-hour training, supervised competency assessment, and certification exam — all provided by ANNA at no cost) and obtain certification within the timeframe set by ANNA's onboarding policy. Certification must be maintained in good standing throughout employment.</p></li></ul><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Available Monday–Friday, 8:00 AM–4:30 PM.</p></li></ul><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Passionate about working with children with Autism and eager to grow in the ABA field.</p></li></ul><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong communication and interpersonal skills.</p></li></ul><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Degree in Psychology, Education, Child Development, or related field preferred (not required).</p></li></ul><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience working with children preferred.</p></li></ul><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Able to perform physically active tasks: sitting on the floor, crawling, running, lifting up to 50 lbs, and maintaining close proximity to clients during sessions.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Apply today! ANNA is an equal opportunity employer and encourages all qualified candidates to apply, even if you don't meet every requirement.</em></p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">ANNA is an equal opportunity employer. We're committed to creating a diverse, inclusive, and supportive workplace. All qualified applicants receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, national origin, age, disability, religion, sex (including pregnancy, sexual orientation, and gender identity), or any other characteristic protected by law. If you're passionate about our mission but don't meet every qualification listed, we still encourage you to apply. Your unique perspective might be exactly what we need.\"</p>","descriptionPlain":"Behavior Therapist (BT) — ABA Therapy\n\nStarting at $24–$26/hr | Full-Time | Monday–Friday, 8:00 AM–4:30 PM | No Evenings or Weekends\n\nANNA Autism Care is hiring passionate Behavior Therapists (BTs) to deliver evidence-based, 1-on-1 therapy to children with Autism using the Naturalistic Developmental Behavioral Intervention (NDBI) approach. Registered Behavior Technician (RBT) certification is a condition of employment for this role — and ANNA makes it easy: we provide the required RBT training and cover the cost of certification at no expense to you, with paid training time and extensive clinical supervision at our center-based Autism care centers across Massachusetts. \n\nWhat ANNA Autism Care Offers:\n\n - Competitive Pay + Retention Bonus: $24–$26/hr starting pay, plus a $400 retention bonus after 6 months of employment.\n\n - Comprehensive Benefits: Health, dental, and vision insurance, 401(k) with company matching, and paid time off.\n\n - Consistent Schedule: Monday–Friday, 8:00 AM–4:30 PM. No evenings, no weekends.\n\n - Full-Time Hours: 25–35 hours per week with a stable clinic-based schedule working with 5–7 clients in a clinical pod.\n\n - Free RBT Certification: ANNA provides the RBT 40-hour training, supervised competency assessment, and first certification exam attempt at no cost to you — with paid training time and a certification bonus for completing your RBT training within 2 weeks of starting.\n\n - Paid Training & Weekly Supervision: Extensive paid onboarding plus weekly clinical supervision and ongoing mentorship from BCBAs.\n\n - Career Advancement: Clear promotion paths for BTs at every stage, including BCBA sponsorship for top performers (Master's in ABA tuition covered by ANNA).\n\n - Supportive Team Culture: Monthly team lunches, seasonal celebrations, summer events, and a community that grows together.\n\nKey Responsibilities:\n\n - Implement individualized ABA therapy plans under BCBA supervision to teach new skills in communication and socialization while reducing any challenging, injurious behaviors.\n\n - Deliver play-based, child-centered therapy using the NDBI framework.\n\n - Collect accurate session data to measure each client's progress toward treatment plan goals, and communicate progress with clinical supervisors.\n\n - Assist BCBAs with assessment procedures (e.g., preference assessments and skill or behavior assessments) as directed.\n\n - Comply with applicable supervision standards, including participating in scheduled BCBA supervision and completing all required supervision and session documentation.\n\n - Obtain and maintain active Registered Behavior Technician (RBT) certification in good standing, including BACB supervision, renewal, and ethics requirements.\n\n - Build positive relationships with children and families, providing caregivers with daily updates.\n\n - Maintain a safe, organized and engaging therapy environment.\n\nQualifications:\n\n - Registered Behavior Technician (RBT) certification — required as a condition of employment. Candidates who are not yet certified must complete ANNA's paid RBT training program (40-hour training, supervised competency assessment, and certification exam — all provided by ANNA at no cost) and obtain certification within the timeframe set by ANNA's onboarding policy. Certification must be maintained in good standing throughout employment.\n\n - Available Monday–Friday, 8:00 AM–4:30 PM.\n\n - Passionate about working with children with Autism and eager to grow in the ABA field.\n\n - Strong communication and interpersonal skills.\n\n - Degree in Psychology, Education, Child Development, or related field preferred (not required).\n\n - Experience working with children preferred.\n\n - Able to perform physically active tasks: sitting on the floor, crawling, running, lifting up to 50 lbs, and maintaining close proximity to clients during sessions.\n\nApply today! ANNA is an equal opportunity employer and encourages all qualified candidates to apply, even if you don't meet every requirement.\n\n \n\nANNA is an equal opportunity employer. We're committed to creating a diverse, inclusive, and supportive workplace. All qualified applicants receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, national origin, age, disability, religion, sex (including pregnancy, sexual orientation, and gender identity), or any other characteristic protected by law. If you're passionate about our mission but don't meet every qualification listed, we still encourage you to apply. Your unique perspective might be exactly what we need.\"","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":"$24 – $26 per hour","scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[{"id":"947cc4ab-53d4-414a-9508-f96bc57ac607","tierSummary":"Billable Hourly Pay $24 – $26 per hour","title":null,"additionalInformation":null,"components":[{"id":"c415085e-d678-49ed-a3c2-b8d042a20408","summary":"Billable Hourly Pay $24 – $26 per hour","compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 HOUR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":24,"maxValue":26}]}],"summaryComponents":[{"compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 HOUR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":24,"maxValue":26}]}},{"id":"a3f4fa8d-27b2-4494-bea0-1c504119f74b","title":"Board Certified Behavior Analyst (BCBA)","department":"Clinical","team":"Board Certified Behavior Analysts","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"Woburn","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-06-03T16:52:38.586+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":false,"workplaceType":"OnSite","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"Massachusetts","addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"Woburn"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/annaautismcare/a3f4fa8d-27b2-4494-bea0-1c504119f74b","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/annaautismcare/a3f4fa8d-27b2-4494-bea0-1c504119f74b/application","descriptionHtml":"<p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Board Certified Behavior Analyst (BCBA) — ABA Therapy</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>$85,000–$115,000/yr + Monthly Bonuses | Full-Time, 40 hrs/wk | Monday–Friday | No Evenings, Weekends, or Travel</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">ANNA Autism Care is seeking an experienced, mission-driven Board Certified Behavior Analyst (BCBA) to join our clinician-led team. We specialize in early intervention ABA therapy for Autistic children under age 6, using the neuroaffirming model, Naturalistic Developmental Behavioral Intervention, or NDBI (ESDM, PRT, JASPER).</p><h2><br /><strong>Why Join ANNA?</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em><strong>Competitive Salary &amp; Monthly Bonuses:</strong> </em>$85K–$115K base salary plus $30/hr for every billable hour over 100/month. Comprehensive health, dental, and vision insurance and 401(k) with company match.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em><strong>Work-Life Balance: </strong></em>40-hour schedule, Monday–Friday. No travel, no evenings, no weekends.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em><strong>Manageable Caseloads: </strong></em>Small, intentional caseloads so you can deliver high-quality clinical care — not just high volume, that adhere to evidence-based autism clinical care and genuine clinical growth.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em><strong>Clinician-Led, Mission-Driven Culture:</strong> </em>Every decision starts with what's best for the child. We stay current with research and hold ourselves to a high clinical standard with our NDBI approach.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em><strong>Strong Team Support:</strong> </em>Regular individual and group supervision from experienced clinicians invested in your success.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em><strong>Professional Development: </strong></em>Annual CEU stipend, conference support, and clear pathways into clinical leadership.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em><strong>Purpose-Built Technology: </strong></em>Streamlined data collection and clinical management tools so you stay focused on clients, not paperwork.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em><strong>Team Culture</strong>: </em>Quarterly outings, milestone celebrations, and a team that genuinely collaborates and enjoys working together.</p><h2><br /><strong>Key Responsibilities:</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em><strong>Assessment &amp; Treatment Planning:</strong> </em>Conduct comprehensive assessments and develop individualized, play-based treatment plans grounded in NDBI strategies for children ages 18 months to 6 years.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em><strong>Supervise &amp; Mentor: </strong></em>Lead and mentor a team of 5 - 6 Behavior Therapists through weekly individual and group supervision, building confident and skilled practitioners.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em><strong>Family Partnership: </strong></em>Implement a structured, curriculum-based parent training model which helps families learn NDBI strategies to practice and use at home.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em><strong>Data-Driven Decision Making:</strong> </em>Monitor client progress through ongoing data collection and analysis, adjusting treatment plans proactively to drive meaningful milestones.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em><strong>Collaborative Care: </strong></em>Work closely with fellow BCBAs and report to a Clinical Director who is invested in both your growth and the quality of care delivered.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em><strong>Clinical Growth: </strong></em>Contribute to a culture of continuous learning by integrating current research and best practices in Autism and ABA therapy.</p><h2><br /><strong>Qualifications:</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em> <strong>BCBA certification (required).</strong></em></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience delivering ABA therapy to young, Autistic children, preferably under age 6.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">NDBI experience preferred (ESDM, PRT, and/or JASPER).</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Commitment to neurodiversity-affirming, evidence-based practice.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong interpersonal skills; ability to work both independently and collaboratively.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Compensation &amp; Benefits:</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Base salary: $85,000–$115,000/year</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Monthly bonus: $30/hr for every billable hour over 100/month</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Health, dental, and vision insurance</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">401(k) with company match</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Paid time off (vacation, sick, and holidays)</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Annual CEU stipend and professional development support</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Apply today and join ANNA Autism Care's mission to modernize early intervention ABA care to a higher standard.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">ANNA is an equal opportunity employer. We're committed to creating a diverse, inclusive, and supportive workplace. All qualified applicants receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, national origin, age, disability, religion, sex (including pregnancy, sexual orientation, and gender identity), or any other characteristic protected by law. If you're passionate about our mission but don't meet every qualification listed, we still encourage you to apply. Your unique perspective might be exactly what we need.\"</p>","descriptionPlain":"Board Certified Behavior Analyst (BCBA) — ABA Therapy\n\n$85,000–$115,000/yr + Monthly Bonuses | Full-Time, 40 hrs/wk | Monday–Friday | No Evenings, Weekends, or Travel\n\nANNA Autism Care is seeking an experienced, mission-driven Board Certified Behavior Analyst (BCBA) to join our clinician-led team. We specialize in early intervention ABA therapy for Autistic children under age 6, using the neuroaffirming model, Naturalistic Developmental Behavioral Intervention, or NDBI (ESDM, PRT, JASPER).\n\n\n\nWHY JOIN ANNA?\n\nCompetitive Salary & Monthly Bonuses: $85K–$115K base salary plus $30/hr for every billable hour over 100/month. Comprehensive health, dental, and vision insurance and 401(k) with company match.\n\nWork-Life Balance: 40-hour schedule, Monday–Friday. No travel, no evenings, no weekends.\n\nManageable Caseloads: Small, intentional caseloads so you can deliver high-quality clinical care — not just high volume, that adhere to evidence-based autism clinical care and genuine clinical growth.\n\nClinician-Led, Mission-Driven Culture: Every decision starts with what's best for the child. We stay current with research and hold ourselves to a high clinical standard with our NDBI approach.\n\nStrong Team Support: Regular individual and group supervision from experienced clinicians invested in your success.\n\nProfessional Development: Annual CEU stipend, conference support, and clear pathways into clinical leadership.\n\nPurpose-Built Technology: Streamlined data collection and clinical management tools so you stay focused on clients, not paperwork.\n\nTeam Culture: Quarterly outings, milestone celebrations, and a team that genuinely collaborates and enjoys working together.\n\n\n\nKEY RESPONSIBILITIES:\n\nAssessment & Treatment Planning: Conduct comprehensive assessments and develop individualized, play-based treatment plans grounded in NDBI strategies for children ages 18 months to 6 years.\n\nSupervise & Mentor: Lead and mentor a team of 5 - 6 Behavior Therapists through weekly individual and group supervision, building confident and skilled practitioners.\n\nFamily Partnership: Implement a structured, curriculum-based parent training model which helps families learn NDBI strategies to practice and use at home.\n\nData-Driven Decision Making: Monitor client progress through ongoing data collection and analysis, adjusting treatment plans proactively to drive meaningful milestones.\n\nCollaborative Care: Work closely with fellow BCBAs and report to a Clinical Director who is invested in both your growth and the quality of care delivered.\n\nClinical Growth: Contribute to a culture of continuous learning by integrating current research and best practices in Autism and ABA therapy.\n\n\n\nQUALIFICATIONS:\n\n BCBA certification (required).\n\n - Experience delivering ABA therapy to young, Autistic children, preferably under age 6.\n\n - NDBI experience preferred (ESDM, PRT, and/or JASPER).\n\n - Commitment to neurodiversity-affirming, evidence-based practice.\n\n - Strong interpersonal skills; ability to work both independently and collaboratively.\n\nCompensation & Benefits:\n\n - Base salary: $85,000–$115,000/year\n\n - Monthly bonus: $30/hr for every billable hour over 100/month\n\n - Health, dental, and vision insurance\n\n - 401(k) with company match\n\n - Paid time off (vacation, sick, and holidays)\n\n - Annual CEU stipend and professional development support\n\nApply today and join ANNA Autism Care's mission to modernize early intervention ABA care to a higher standard.\n\nANNA is an equal opportunity employer. We're committed to creating a diverse, inclusive, and supportive workplace. All qualified applicants receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, national origin, age, disability, religion, sex (including pregnancy, sexual orientation, and gender identity), or any other characteristic protected by law. If you're passionate about our mission but don't meet every qualification listed, we still encourage you to apply. Your unique perspective might be exactly what we need.\"","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"d8eddc63-6f51-4e3c-ac46-a29b5df0e81c","title":"Board Certified Behavior Analyst (BCBA)","department":"Clinical","team":"Board Certified Behavior Analysts","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"Weston","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-08-21T20:00:42.999+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":false,"workplaceType":"OnSite","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"Massachusetts","addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"Weston"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/annaautismcare/d8eddc63-6f51-4e3c-ac46-a29b5df0e81c","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/annaautismcare/d8eddc63-6f51-4e3c-ac46-a29b5df0e81c/application","descriptionHtml":"<p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Board Certified Behavior Analyst (BCBA) — ABA Therapy</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>$85,000–$115,000/yr + Monthly Bonuses | Full-Time, 40 hrs/wk | Monday–Friday | No Evenings, Weekends, or Travel</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">ANNA Autism Care is seeking an experienced, mission-driven Board Certified Behavior Analyst (BCBA) to join our clinician-led team. We specialize in early intervention ABA therapy for Autistic children under age 6, using the neuroaffirming model, Naturalistic Developmental Behavioral Intervention, or NDBI (ESDM, PRT, JASPER).</p><h2><br /><strong>Why Join ANNA?</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Competitive Salary &amp; Monthly Bonuses: </em>$85K–$115K base salary plus $30/hr for every billable hour over 100/month. Comprehensive health, dental, and vision insurance and 401(k) with company match.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Work-Life Balance: </em>40-hour schedule, Monday–Friday. No travel, no evenings, no weekends.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Manageable Caseloads: </em>Small, intentional caseloads so you can deliver high-quality clinical care — not just high volume, that adhere to evidence-based autism clinical care and genuine clinical growth.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Clinician-Led, Mission-Driven Culture: </em>Every decision starts with what's best for the child. We stay current with research and hold ourselves to a high clinical standard with our NDBI approach.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Strong Team Support: </em>Regular individual and group supervision from experienced clinicians invested in your success.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Professional Development: </em>Annual CEU stipend, conference support, and clear pathways into clinical leadership.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Purpose-Built Technology: </em>Streamlined data collection and clinical management tools so you stay focused on clients, not paperwork.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Team Culture: </em>Quarterly outings, milestone celebrations, and a team that genuinely collaborates and enjoys working together.</p><h2><br /><strong>Key Responsibilities:</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Assessment &amp; Treatment Planning: </em>Conduct comprehensive assessments and develop individualized, play-based treatment plans grounded in NDBI strategies for children ages 18 months to 6 years.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Supervise &amp; Mentor: </em>Lead and mentor a team of 5 - 6 Behavior Therapists through weekly individual and group supervision, building confident and skilled practitioners.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Family Partnership: </em>Implement a structured, curriculum-based parent training model which helps families learn NDBI strategies to practice and use at home.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Data-Driven Decision Making: </em>Monitor client progress through ongoing data collection and analysis, adjusting treatment plans proactively to drive meaningful milestones.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Collaborative Care: </em>Work closely with fellow BCBAs and report to a Clinical Director who is invested in both your growth and the quality of care delivered.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Clinical Growth: </em>Contribute to a culture of continuous learning by integrating current research and best practices in Autism and ABA therapy.</p><h2><br /><strong>Qualifications:</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em> <strong>BCBA certification (required).</strong></em></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience delivering ABA therapy to young, Autistic children, preferably under age 6.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">NDBI experience preferred (ESDM, PRT, and/or JASPER).</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Commitment to neurodiversity-affirming, evidence-based practice.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong interpersonal skills; ability to work both independently and collaboratively.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Compensation &amp; Benefits:</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Base salary: $85,000–$115,000/year</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Monthly bonus: $30/hr for every billable hour over 100/month</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Health, dental, and vision insurance</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">401(k) with company match</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Paid time off (vacation, sick, and holidays)</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Annual CEU stipend and professional development support</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Apply today and join ANNA Autism Care's mission to modernize early intervention ABA care to a higher standard.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">ANNA is an equal opportunity employer. We're committed to creating a diverse, inclusive, and supportive workplace. All qualified applicants receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, national origin, age, disability, religion, sex (including pregnancy, sexual orientation, and gender identity), or any other characteristic protected by law. If you're passionate about our mission but don't meet every qualification listed, we still encourage you to apply. Your unique perspective might be exactly what we need.\"</p>","descriptionPlain":"Board Certified Behavior Analyst (BCBA) — ABA Therapy\n\n$85,000–$115,000/yr + Monthly Bonuses | Full-Time, 40 hrs/wk | Monday–Friday | No Evenings, Weekends, or Travel\n\nANNA Autism Care is seeking an experienced, mission-driven Board Certified Behavior Analyst (BCBA) to join our clinician-led team. We specialize in early intervention ABA therapy for Autistic children under age 6, using the neuroaffirming model, Naturalistic Developmental Behavioral Intervention, or NDBI (ESDM, PRT, JASPER).\n\n\n\nWHY JOIN ANNA?\n\nCompetitive Salary & Monthly Bonuses: $85K–$115K base salary plus $30/hr for every billable hour over 100/month. Comprehensive health, dental, and vision insurance and 401(k) with company match.\n\nWork-Life Balance: 40-hour schedule, Monday–Friday. No travel, no evenings, no weekends.\n\nManageable Caseloads: Small, intentional caseloads so you can deliver high-quality clinical care — not just high volume, that adhere to evidence-based autism clinical care and genuine clinical growth.\n\nClinician-Led, Mission-Driven Culture: Every decision starts with what's best for the child. We stay current with research and hold ourselves to a high clinical standard with our NDBI approach.\n\nStrong Team Support: Regular individual and group supervision from experienced clinicians invested in your success.\n\nProfessional Development: Annual CEU stipend, conference support, and clear pathways into clinical leadership.\n\nPurpose-Built Technology: Streamlined data collection and clinical management tools so you stay focused on clients, not paperwork.\n\nTeam Culture: Quarterly outings, milestone celebrations, and a team that genuinely collaborates and enjoys working together.\n\n\n\nKEY RESPONSIBILITIES:\n\nAssessment & Treatment Planning: Conduct comprehensive assessments and develop individualized, play-based treatment plans grounded in NDBI strategies for children ages 18 months to 6 years.\n\nSupervise & Mentor: Lead and mentor a team of 5 - 6 Behavior Therapists through weekly individual and group supervision, building confident and skilled practitioners.\n\nFamily Partnership: Implement a structured, curriculum-based parent training model which helps families learn NDBI strategies to practice and use at home.\n\nData-Driven Decision Making: Monitor client progress through ongoing data collection and analysis, adjusting treatment plans proactively to drive meaningful milestones.\n\nCollaborative Care: Work closely with fellow BCBAs and report to a Clinical Director who is invested in both your growth and the quality of care delivered.\n\nClinical Growth: Contribute to a culture of continuous learning by integrating current research and best practices in Autism and ABA therapy.\n\n\n\nQUALIFICATIONS:\n\n BCBA certification (required).\n\n - Experience delivering ABA therapy to young, Autistic children, preferably under age 6.\n\n - NDBI experience preferred (ESDM, PRT, and/or JASPER).\n\n - Commitment to neurodiversity-affirming, evidence-based practice.\n\n - Strong interpersonal skills; ability to work both independently and collaboratively.\n\nCompensation & Benefits:\n\n - Base salary: $85,000–$115,000/year\n\n - Monthly bonus: $30/hr for every billable hour over 100/month\n\n - Health, dental, and vision insurance\n\n - 401(k) with company match\n\n - Paid time off (vacation, sick, and holidays)\n\n - Annual CEU stipend and professional development support\n\nApply today and join ANNA Autism Care's mission to modernize early intervention ABA care to a higher standard.\n\nANNA is an equal opportunity employer. We're committed to creating a diverse, inclusive, and supportive workplace. All qualified applicants receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, national origin, age, disability, religion, sex (including pregnancy, sexual orientation, and gender identity), or any other characteristic protected by law. If you're passionate about our mission but don't meet every qualification listed, we still encourage you to apply. Your unique perspective might be exactly what we need.\"","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"73256273-29fa-484f-b8e4-bc810540c8d2","title":"Behavior Therapist ","department":"Clinical","team":"Behavior Therapists","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"Weston","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":true,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-07-16T19:50:26.740+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":false,"workplaceType":"OnSite","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"Massachusetts","addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"Weston"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/annaautismcare/73256273-29fa-484f-b8e4-bc810540c8d2","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/annaautismcare/73256273-29fa-484f-b8e4-bc810540c8d2/application","descriptionHtml":"<p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Behavior Therapist (BT) — ABA Therapy</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Starting at $24–$26/hr | Full-Time | Monday–Friday, 8:00 AM–4:30 PM | No Evenings or Weekends</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">ANNA Autism Care is hiring passionate Behavior Therapists (BTs) to deliver evidence-based, 1-on-1 therapy to children with Autism using the Naturalistic Developmental Behavioral Intervention (NDBI) approach. Registered Behavior Technician (RBT) certification is a condition of employment for this role — and ANNA makes it easy: we provide the required RBT training and cover the cost of certification at no expense to you, with paid training time and extensive clinical supervision at our center-based Autism care centers across Massachusetts. </p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>What ANNA Autism Care Offers:</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Competitive Pay + Retention Bonus</em>: $24–$26/hr starting pay, plus a $400 retention bonus after 6 months of employment.</p></li></ul><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Comprehensive Benefits:</em> Health, dental, and vision insurance, 401(k) with company matching, and paid time off.</p></li></ul><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Consistent Schedule:</em> Monday–Friday, 8:00 AM–4:30 PM. No evenings, no weekends.</p></li></ul><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Full-Time Hours: </em>25–35 hours per week with a stable clinic-based schedule working with 5–7 clients in a clinical pod.</p></li></ul><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Free RBT Certification:</em> ANNA provides the RBT 40-hour training, supervised competency assessment, and first certification exam attempt at no cost to you — with paid training time and a certification bonus for completing your RBT training within 2 weeks of starting.</p></li></ul><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">P<em>aid Training &amp; Weekly Supervision:</em> Extensive paid onboarding plus weekly clinical supervision and ongoing mentorship from BCBAs.</p></li></ul><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Career Advancement: </em>Clear promotion paths for BTs at every stage, including BCBA sponsorship for top performers (Master's in ABA tuition covered by ANNA).</p></li></ul><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Supportive Team Culture: </em>Monthly team lunches, seasonal celebrations, summer events, and a community that grows together.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Key Responsibilities:</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Implement individualized ABA therapy plans under BCBA supervision to teach new skills in communication and socialization while reducing any challenging, injurious behaviors.</p></li></ul><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Deliver play-based, child-centered therapy using the NDBI framework.</p></li></ul><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Collect accurate session data to measure each client's progress toward treatment plan goals, and communicate progress with clinical supervisors.</p></li></ul><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Assist BCBAs with assessment procedures (e.g., preference assessments and skill or behavior assessments) as directed.</p></li></ul><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Comply with applicable supervision standards, including participating in scheduled BCBA supervision and completing all required supervision and session documentation.</p></li></ul><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Obtain and maintain active Registered Behavior Technician (RBT) certification in good standing, including BACB supervision, renewal, and ethics requirements.</p></li></ul><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Build positive relationships with children and families, providing caregivers with daily updates.</p></li></ul><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Maintain a safe, organized and engaging therapy environment.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Qualifications:</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Registered Behavior Technician (RBT) certification — required as a condition of employment. </strong>Candidates who are not yet certified must complete ANNA's paid RBT training program (40-hour training, supervised competency assessment, and certification exam — all provided by ANNA at no cost) and obtain certification within the timeframe set by ANNA's onboarding policy. Certification must be maintained in good standing throughout employment.</p></li></ul><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Available Monday–Friday, 8:00 AM–4:30 PM.</p></li></ul><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Passionate about working with children with Autism and eager to grow in the ABA field.</p></li></ul><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong communication and interpersonal skills.</p></li></ul><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Degree in Psychology, Education, Child Development, or related field preferred (not required).</p></li></ul><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience working with children preferred.</p></li></ul><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Able to perform physically active tasks: sitting on the floor, crawling, running, lifting up to 50 lbs, and maintaining close proximity to clients during sessions.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Apply today! ANNA is an equal opportunity employer and encourages all qualified candidates to apply, even if you don't meet every requirement.</em></p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">ANNA is an equal opportunity employer. We're committed to creating a diverse, inclusive, and supportive workplace. All qualified applicants receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, national origin, age, disability, religion, sex (including pregnancy, sexual orientation, and gender identity), or any other characteristic protected by law. If you're passionate about our mission but don't meet every qualification listed, we still encourage you to apply. Your unique perspective might be exactly what we need.\"</p>","descriptionPlain":"Behavior Therapist (BT) — ABA Therapy\n\nStarting at $24–$26/hr | Full-Time | Monday–Friday, 8:00 AM–4:30 PM | No Evenings or Weekends\n\nANNA Autism Care is hiring passionate Behavior Therapists (BTs) to deliver evidence-based, 1-on-1 therapy to children with Autism using the Naturalistic Developmental Behavioral Intervention (NDBI) approach. Registered Behavior Technician (RBT) certification is a condition of employment for this role — and ANNA makes it easy: we provide the required RBT training and cover the cost of certification at no expense to you, with paid training time and extensive clinical supervision at our center-based Autism care centers across Massachusetts. \n\nWhat ANNA Autism Care Offers:\n\n - Competitive Pay + Retention Bonus: $24–$26/hr starting pay, plus a $400 retention bonus after 6 months of employment.\n\n - Comprehensive Benefits: Health, dental, and vision insurance, 401(k) with company matching, and paid time off.\n\n - Consistent Schedule: Monday–Friday, 8:00 AM–4:30 PM. No evenings, no weekends.\n\n - Full-Time Hours: 25–35 hours per week with a stable clinic-based schedule working with 5–7 clients in a clinical pod.\n\n - Free RBT Certification: ANNA provides the RBT 40-hour training, supervised competency assessment, and first certification exam attempt at no cost to you — with paid training time and a certification bonus for completing your RBT training within 2 weeks of starting.\n\n - Paid Training & Weekly Supervision: Extensive paid onboarding plus weekly clinical supervision and ongoing mentorship from BCBAs.\n\n - Career Advancement: Clear promotion paths for BTs at every stage, including BCBA sponsorship for top performers (Master's in ABA tuition covered by ANNA).\n\n - Supportive Team Culture: Monthly team lunches, seasonal celebrations, summer events, and a community that grows together.\n\nKey Responsibilities:\n\n - Implement individualized ABA therapy plans under BCBA supervision to teach new skills in communication and socialization while reducing any challenging, injurious behaviors.\n\n - Deliver play-based, child-centered therapy using the NDBI framework.\n\n - Collect accurate session data to measure each client's progress toward treatment plan goals, and communicate progress with clinical supervisors.\n\n - Assist BCBAs with assessment procedures (e.g., preference assessments and skill or behavior assessments) as directed.\n\n - Comply with applicable supervision standards, including participating in scheduled BCBA supervision and completing all required supervision and session documentation.\n\n - Obtain and maintain active Registered Behavior Technician (RBT) certification in good standing, including BACB supervision, renewal, and ethics requirements.\n\n - Build positive relationships with children and families, providing caregivers with daily updates.\n\n - Maintain a safe, organized and engaging therapy environment.\n\nQualifications:\n\n - Registered Behavior Technician (RBT) certification — required as a condition of employment. Candidates who are not yet certified must complete ANNA's paid RBT training program (40-hour training, supervised competency assessment, and certification exam — all provided by ANNA at no cost) and obtain certification within the timeframe set by ANNA's onboarding policy. Certification must be maintained in good standing throughout employment.\n\n - Available Monday–Friday, 8:00 AM–4:30 PM.\n\n - Passionate about working with children with Autism and eager to grow in the ABA field.\n\n - Strong communication and interpersonal skills.\n\n - Degree in Psychology, Education, Child Development, or related field preferred (not required).\n\n - Experience working with children preferred.\n\n - Able to perform physically active tasks: sitting on the floor, crawling, running, lifting up to 50 lbs, and maintaining close proximity to clients during sessions.\n\nApply today! ANNA is an equal opportunity employer and encourages all qualified candidates to apply, even if you don't meet every requirement.\n\n \n\nANNA is an equal opportunity employer. We're committed to creating a diverse, inclusive, and supportive workplace. All qualified applicants receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, national origin, age, disability, religion, sex (including pregnancy, sexual orientation, and gender identity), or any other characteristic protected by law. If you're passionate about our mission but don't meet every qualification listed, we still encourage you to apply. Your unique perspective might be exactly what we need.\"","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":"$24 – $26 per hour","scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[{"id":"14f72786-b965-44ef-b12a-9dc2dbab2e1d","tierSummary":"Billable Hourly Pay $24 – $26 per hour","title":null,"additionalInformation":null,"components":[{"id":"d85883e0-5595-4478-b0fe-877976be3197","summary":"Billable Hourly Pay $24 – $26 per hour","compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 HOUR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":24,"maxValue":26}]}],"summaryComponents":[{"compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 HOUR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":24,"maxValue":26}]}},{"id":"2a3fd0c4-b6dd-40fb-a0d2-fd0912e99351","title":"Senior Salesforce Administrator","department":"Support Team","team":"Support Team","employmentType":"Contract","location":"Remote - Philippines","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":true,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-07-16T12:54:57.794+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Remote","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressCountry":"Philippines"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/annaautismcare/2a3fd0c4-b6dd-40fb-a0d2-fd0912e99351","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/annaautismcare/2a3fd0c4-b6dd-40fb-a0d2-fd0912e99351/application","descriptionHtml":"<h1><strong>ANNA Autism Care</strong></h1><h2><strong>Senior Salesforce Administrator</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Remote (Philippines) | Hourly Contract, US Eastern Hours</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">$12 – $15 USD per hour, commensurate with experience and relevant certifications</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><h1>About ANNA</h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">ANNA (Allied Network for Neurodevelopmental Advancement) is a mission-driven organization that provides ABA services to young autistic children (under the age of 6) and their families using a neurodiversity-affirming, Naturalistic Developmental Behavioral Intervention (NDBI) approach. We operate center-based clinics across Massachusetts and Missouri and are growing quickly — and we're looking for a deeply technical Senior Salesforce Administrator to own and evolve the platform at the heart of our clinical and business operations.</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><h1>Position Overview</h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">The Senior Salesforce Administrator owns and evolves ANNA's Salesforce ecosystem, which is built on Lumary (a Salesforce OEM) and supports clinical service delivery, referrals, business development, and operational workflows across our markets. This is not a basic “clicks-and-tickets” admin position — you are the technical owner of deep configuration, automation, data architecture, security, and system reliability in a regulated, HIPAA-sensitive environment.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Based in the Philippines and working contracted hours anchored to US Eastern Time, you will partner closely with operations, clinical leadership, and product/engineering to ensure Salesforce is scalable, compliant, and aligned with real-world healthcare workflows — including partnering with internal technology teams on AI-driven capabilities as ANNA builds out its agentic infrastructure.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This role reports directly to our Co-Founder &amp; CEO. Success is measured by platform stability and performance, smooth and low-risk Lumary releases, high and auditable data quality, reporting the whole organization trusts and uses, and stakeholders treating you as the system owner — not just a support resource.</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><h1>Compensation &amp; Engagement</h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Hourly Rate</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">$12 – $15 USD per hour (based on experience and certifications)</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Guaranteed Retainer</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">80 hours per month minimum, billed monthly whether fully utilized or not</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Overage</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Additional hours billed at the same rate; pre-approval required above 100 hours/month</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Engagement Type</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Independent contractor — remote, with core availability during US Eastern hours</p></li></ul><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><h1>What You'll Do</h1><h2><em><strong>Salesforce &amp; Lumary Platform Ownership</strong></em></h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Own day-to-day administration of Salesforce (Enterprise) with Lumary-managed packages and OEM constraints</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Configure and maintain complex objects, record types, page layouts, dynamic forms, flows, validation rules, and permissions within Lumary's data model</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Understand and work within Lumary package limitations, upgrade paths, and dependency constraints without breaking managed components</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Act as the technical owner for Lumary releases, sandbox testing, regression testing, and production deployments</p></li></ul><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><h2><em><strong>Automation &amp; System Logic</strong></em></h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Design, build, and maintain advanced Salesforce Flows (record-triggered, screen flows, scheduled flows)</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Replace legacy workflow/process builder logic with optimized Flow-based automation</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Implement robust error handling, logging, and guardrails to prevent data corruption</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Partner with developers when Apex is required, but independently handle 90%+ of automation via configuration</p></li></ul><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><h2><em><strong>Data Architecture &amp; Integrity</strong></em></h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Own Salesforce data model health: relationships, indexing strategy, field usage, and scalability</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Design and maintain data validation frameworks to ensure clinical, billing, and operational data accuracy</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Manage data imports, exports, and transformations using tools such as Data Loader and Workbench, accounting for PHI sensitivity</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Lead deduplication strategies and data quality monitoring</p></li></ul><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><h2><em><strong>Security, Compliance &amp; Access Control</strong></em></h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Implement and maintain role hierarchies, permission sets, permission set groups, sharing rules, and field-level security</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ensure Salesforce configuration aligns with HIPAA-compliant workflows (least privilege, auditability, access traceability)</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Partner with leadership to support audits, internal controls, and compliance reviews</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Manage login security, MFA enforcement, session settings, and connected app access</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div></li></ul><h2><em><strong>Integrations &amp; System Operations</strong></em></h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Support and monitor integrations between Salesforce/Lumary and external systems (e.g., EHR, billing, scheduling, reporting tools)</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Troubleshoot integration failures using logs, debug tools, and data inspection</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Coordinate with vendors and internal engineers on API-based workflows and data syncs</p></li></ul><h2><em>Reporting &amp; Insights</em></h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Build and maintain advanced reports and dashboards for operational, clinical, and leadership use</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ensure reporting accuracy given Lumary's managed objects and relationships</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Partner with stakeholders to translate business questions into reliable Salesforce analytics</p></li></ul><h2><em>Stakeholder Enablement</em></h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Act as a technical advisor to operations, clinical teams, and leadership</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Translate complex requirements into scalable Salesforce solutions</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Create clear documentation for system behavior, data definitions, and admin processes</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Provide tier-2/3 support for escalated Salesforce issues</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Partner with internal technology teams on AI-driven capabilities — surfacing Salesforce/Lumary data to agentic workflows and identifying where AI reduces admin toil</p></li></ul><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><h1>Qualifications</h1><h2><em>Required</em></h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">4+ years of hands-on Salesforce Administration experience in complex orgs</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Demonstrated ability to work US Eastern Time hours (approx. 9 PM – 6 AM Manila time, including DST shifts) for contracted coverage windows</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Deep expertise in Salesforce Flow (advanced), permission models &amp; security architecture, data modeling and schema design, and change management across sandboxes</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience working with Salesforce managed packages, ideally OEM products</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Salesforce Administrator Certification required; Advanced Admin or Platform App Builder strongly preferred</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong debugging and root-cause analysis skills</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience supporting Salesforce integrations (REST APIs, middleware, or vendor-managed integrations)</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Demonstrated AI fluency — comfort using Claude or similar tools daily for debugging, documentation, and workflow design</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Excellent written documentation and communication skills; ability to operate independently and make sound technical decisions</p></li></ul><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><h2><em>Preferred</em></h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Prior experience with Lumary, Salesforce Health Cloud, or healthcare-focused Salesforce implementations</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Understanding of healthcare service workflows, compliance considerations, and data sensitivity; comfort operating in regulated environments with strict access and audit requirements</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience in healthcare services, behavioral health, or care delivery organizations</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Exposure to Apex (reading/debugging), SOQL, and Salesforce deployment tools</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience supporting multi-org or multi-brand Salesforce environments</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Familiarity with OEM product constraints and release management</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>If you don't meet every preferred qualification, we still encourage you to apply. Your unique perspective might be exactly what we need.</em></p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><h1>Ideal Candidate</h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You are a deeply technical Salesforce owner who treats the platform like a product, not a queue. You're fluent in the unglamorous things that make regulated systems trustworthy — permission architecture, validation frameworks, release discipline — and equally strong at translating business questions into schema and automation. You're energized by owning a system end-to-end in a fast-scaling healthcare company, and by working at a company that expects AI to be part of how you work, not a threat to it.</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><h1>Why ANNA?</h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At ANNA, we are working to transform autism care by combining rigorous clinical training, compassionate family-centered practice, and neurodiversity-affirming approaches. Our Naturalistic Developmental Behavioral Intervention (NDBI) model supports each child's strengths through play-based, developmentally informed care.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">As our Senior Salesforce Administrator, you'll own the platform that connects referrals, clinical delivery, and business operations — the system our teams rely on every day to get children into care faster.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You can learn more about us here: <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://annaautismcare.com/about-us/\">https://annaautismcare.com/about-us/</a></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Location:</strong><em> Remote, (Philippines) — hourly contract with core availability during US Eastern Time hours</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>ANNA Autism Care | Senior Salesforce Administrator</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">ANNA is an equal opportunity employer. We're committed to creating a diverse, inclusive, and supportive workplace. All qualified applicants receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, national origin, age, disability, religion, sex (including pregnancy, sexual orientation, and gender identity), or any other characteristic protected by law. If you're passionate about our mission but don't meet every qualification listed, we still encourage you to apply. Your unique perspective might be exactly what we need.\"</p>","descriptionPlain":"ANNA AUTISM CARE\n\n\nSENIOR SALESFORCE ADMINISTRATOR\n\nRemote (Philippines) | Hourly Contract, US Eastern Hours\n\n$12 – $15 USD per hour, commensurate with experience and relevant certifications\n\n \n\n\nABOUT ANNA\n\nANNA (Allied Network for Neurodevelopmental Advancement) is a mission-driven organization that provides ABA services to young autistic children (under the age of 6) and their families using a neurodiversity-affirming, Naturalistic Developmental Behavioral Intervention (NDBI) approach. We operate center-based clinics across Massachusetts and Missouri and are growing quickly — and we're looking for a deeply technical Senior Salesforce Administrator to own and evolve the platform at the heart of our clinical and business operations.\n\n \n\n\nPOSITION OVERVIEW\n\nThe Senior Salesforce Administrator owns and evolves ANNA's Salesforce ecosystem, which is built on Lumary (a Salesforce OEM) and supports clinical service delivery, referrals, business development, and operational workflows across our markets. This is not a basic “clicks-and-tickets” admin position — you are the technical owner of deep configuration, automation, data architecture, security, and system reliability in a regulated, HIPAA-sensitive environment.\n\nBased in the Philippines and working contracted hours anchored to US Eastern Time, you will partner closely with operations, clinical leadership, and product/engineering to ensure Salesforce is scalable, compliant, and aligned with real-world healthcare workflows — including partnering with internal technology teams on AI-driven capabilities as ANNA builds out its agentic infrastructure.\n\nThis role reports directly to our Co-Founder & CEO. Success is measured by platform stability and performance, smooth and low-risk Lumary releases, high and auditable data quality, reporting the whole organization trusts and uses, and stakeholders treating you as the system owner — not just a support resource.\n\n \n \n\n\nCOMPENSATION & ENGAGEMENT\n\nHourly Rate\n\n - $12 – $15 USD per hour (based on experience and certifications)\n\nGuaranteed Retainer\n\n - 80 hours per month minimum, billed monthly whether fully utilized or not\n\nOverage\n\n - Additional hours billed at the same rate; pre-approval required above 100 hours/month\n\nEngagement Type\n\n - Independent contractor — remote, with core availability during US Eastern hours\n\n \n\n\nWHAT YOU'LL DO\n\n\nSALESFORCE & LUMARY PLATFORM OWNERSHIP\n\n - Own day-to-day administration of Salesforce (Enterprise) with Lumary-managed packages and OEM constraints\n\n - Configure and maintain complex objects, record types, page layouts, dynamic forms, flows, validation rules, and permissions within Lumary's data model\n\n - Understand and work within Lumary package limitations, upgrade paths, and dependency constraints without breaking managed components\n\n - Act as the technical owner for Lumary releases, sandbox testing, regression testing, and production deployments\n\n \n\n\nAUTOMATION & SYSTEM LOGIC\n\n - Design, build, and maintain advanced Salesforce Flows (record-triggered, screen flows, scheduled flows)\n\n - Replace legacy workflow/process builder logic with optimized Flow-based automation\n\n - Implement robust error handling, logging, and guardrails to prevent data corruption\n\n - Partner with developers when Apex is required, but independently handle 90%+ of automation via configuration\n\n \n\n\nDATA ARCHITECTURE & INTEGRITY\n\n - Own Salesforce data model health: relationships, indexing strategy, field usage, and scalability\n\n - Design and maintain data validation frameworks to ensure clinical, billing, and operational data accuracy\n\n - Manage data imports, exports, and transformations using tools such as Data Loader and Workbench, accounting for PHI sensitivity\n\n - Lead deduplication strategies and data quality monitoring\n\n \n\n\nSECURITY, COMPLIANCE & ACCESS CONTROL\n\n - Implement and maintain role hierarchies, permission sets, permission set groups, sharing rules, and field-level security\n\n - Ensure Salesforce configuration aligns with HIPAA-compliant workflows (least privilege, auditability, access traceability)\n\n - Partner with leadership to support audits, internal controls, and compliance reviews\n\n - Manage login security, MFA enforcement, session settings, and connected app access\n   \n    \n\n\nINTEGRATIONS & SYSTEM OPERATIONS\n\n - Support and monitor integrations between Salesforce/Lumary and external systems (e.g., EHR, billing, scheduling, reporting tools)\n\n - Troubleshoot integration failures using logs, debug tools, and data inspection\n\n - Coordinate with vendors and internal engineers on API-based workflows and data syncs\n\n\nREPORTING & INSIGHTS\n\n - Build and maintain advanced reports and dashboards for operational, clinical, and leadership use\n\n - Ensure reporting accuracy given Lumary's managed objects and relationships\n\n - Partner with stakeholders to translate business questions into reliable Salesforce analytics\n\n\nSTAKEHOLDER ENABLEMENT\n\n - Act as a technical advisor to operations, clinical teams, and leadership\n\n - Translate complex requirements into scalable Salesforce solutions\n\n - Create clear documentation for system behavior, data definitions, and admin processes\n\n - Provide tier-2/3 support for escalated Salesforce issues\n\n - Partner with internal technology teams on AI-driven capabilities — surfacing Salesforce/Lumary data to agentic workflows and identifying where AI reduces admin toil\n\n \n\n\nQUALIFICATIONS\n\n\nREQUIRED\n\n - 4+ years of hands-on Salesforce Administration experience in complex orgs\n\n - Demonstrated ability to work US Eastern Time hours (approx. 9 PM – 6 AM Manila time, including DST shifts) for contracted coverage windows\n\n - Deep expertise in Salesforce Flow (advanced), permission models & security architecture, data modeling and schema design, and change management across sandboxes\n\n - Experience working with Salesforce managed packages, ideally OEM products\n\n - Salesforce Administrator Certification required; Advanced Admin or Platform App Builder strongly preferred\n\n - Strong debugging and root-cause analysis skills\n\n - Experience supporting Salesforce integrations (REST APIs, middleware, or vendor-managed integrations)\n\n - Demonstrated AI fluency — comfort using Claude or similar tools daily for debugging, documentation, and workflow design\n\n - Excellent written documentation and communication skills; ability to operate independently and make sound technical decisions\n\n \n\n\nPREFERRED\n\n - Prior experience with Lumary, Salesforce Health Cloud, or healthcare-focused Salesforce implementations\n\n - Understanding of healthcare service workflows, compliance considerations, and data sensitivity; comfort operating in regulated environments with strict access and audit requirements\n\n - Experience in healthcare services, behavioral health, or care delivery organizations\n\n - Exposure to Apex (reading/debugging), SOQL, and Salesforce deployment tools\n\n - Experience supporting multi-org or multi-brand Salesforce environments\n\n - Familiarity with OEM product constraints and release management\n\nIf you don't meet every preferred qualification, we still encourage you to apply. Your unique perspective might be exactly what we need.\n\n \n\n\nIDEAL CANDIDATE\n\nYou are a deeply technical Salesforce owner who treats the platform like a product, not a queue. You're fluent in the unglamorous things that make regulated systems trustworthy — permission architecture, validation frameworks, release discipline — and equally strong at translating business questions into schema and automation. You're energized by owning a system end-to-end in a fast-scaling healthcare company, and by working at a company that expects AI to be part of how you work, not a threat to it.\n\n \n\n\nWHY ANNA?\n\nAt ANNA, we are working to transform autism care by combining rigorous clinical training, compassionate family-centered practice, and neurodiversity-affirming approaches. Our Naturalistic Developmental Behavioral Intervention (NDBI) model supports each child's strengths through play-based, developmentally informed care.\n\nAs our Senior Salesforce Administrator, you'll own the platform that connects referrals, clinical delivery, and business operations — the system our teams rely on every day to get children into care faster.\n\nYou can learn more about us here: https://annaautismcare.com/about-us/\n\n\n\nLocation: Remote, (Philippines) — hourly contract with core availability during US Eastern Time hours\n\n\n\nANNA Autism Care | Senior Salesforce Administrator\n\n\n\nANNA is an equal opportunity employer. We're committed to creating a diverse, inclusive, and supportive workplace. All qualified applicants receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, national origin, age, disability, religion, sex (including pregnancy, sexual orientation, and gender identity), or any other characteristic protected by law. If you're passionate about our mission but don't meet every qualification listed, we still encourage you to apply. Your unique perspective might be exactly what we need.\"","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":"$12 – $15 per hour","scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[{"id":"9ba37f1b-ddac-49bc-b402-df4082d5ae71","tierSummary":"$12 – $15 per hour","title":null,"additionalInformation":null,"components":[{"id":"76d99520-e119-44fa-800b-1aea3336b3fc","summary":"$12 – $15 per hour","compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 HOUR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":12,"maxValue":15}]}],"summaryComponents":[{"compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 HOUR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":12,"maxValue":15}]}},{"id":"7d3d3316-1c3a-4f73-84a9-dbbac8251485","title":"Behavior Therapist ","department":"Clinical","team":"Behavior Therapists","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"Sudbury","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":true,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-06-03T16:42:52.008+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":false,"workplaceType":"OnSite","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"Massachusetts","addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"Sudbury"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/annaautismcare/7d3d3316-1c3a-4f73-84a9-dbbac8251485","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/annaautismcare/7d3d3316-1c3a-4f73-84a9-dbbac8251485/application","descriptionHtml":"<p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Behavior Therapist (BT) — ABA Therapy</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Starting at $24–$26/hr | Full-Time | Monday–Friday, 8:00 AM–4:30 PM | No Evenings or Weekends</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">ANNA Autism Care is hiring passionate Behavior Therapists (BTs) to deliver evidence-based, 1-on-1 therapy to children with Autism using the Naturalistic Developmental Behavioral Intervention (NDBI) approach. Registered Behavior Technician (RBT) certification is a condition of employment for this role — and ANNA makes it easy: we provide the required RBT training and cover the cost of certification at no expense to you, with paid training time and extensive clinical supervision at our center-based Autism care centers across Massachusetts. </p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>What ANNA Autism Care Offers:</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Competitive Pay + Retention Bonus</em>: $24–$26/hr starting pay, plus a $400 retention bonus after 6 months of employment.</p></li></ul><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Comprehensive Benefits:</em> Health, dental, and vision insurance, 401(k) with company matching, and paid time off.</p></li></ul><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Consistent Schedule:</em> Monday–Friday, 8:00 AM–4:30 PM. No evenings, no weekends.</p></li></ul><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Full-Time Hours: </em>25–35 hours per week with a stable clinic-based schedule working with 5–7 clients in a clinical pod.</p></li></ul><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Free RBT Certification:</em> ANNA provides the RBT 40-hour training, supervised competency assessment, and first certification exam attempt at no cost to you — with paid training time and a certification bonus for completing your RBT training within 2 weeks of starting.</p></li></ul><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">P<em>aid Training &amp; Weekly Supervision:</em> Extensive paid onboarding plus weekly clinical supervision and ongoing mentorship from BCBAs.</p></li></ul><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Career Advancement: </em>Clear promotion paths for BTs at every stage, including BCBA sponsorship for top performers (Master's in ABA tuition covered by ANNA).</p></li></ul><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Supportive Team Culture: </em>Monthly team lunches, seasonal celebrations, summer events, and a community that grows together.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Key Responsibilities:</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Implement individualized ABA therapy plans under BCBA supervision to teach new skills in communication and socialization while reducing any challenging, injurious behaviors.</p></li></ul><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Deliver play-based, child-centered therapy using the NDBI framework.</p></li></ul><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Collect accurate session data to measure each client's progress toward treatment plan goals, and communicate progress with clinical supervisors.</p></li></ul><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Assist BCBAs with assessment procedures (e.g., preference assessments and skill or behavior assessments) as directed.</p></li></ul><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Comply with applicable supervision standards, including participating in scheduled BCBA supervision and completing all required supervision and session documentation.</p></li></ul><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Obtain and maintain active Registered Behavior Technician (RBT) certification in good standing, including BACB supervision, renewal, and ethics requirements.</p></li></ul><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Build positive relationships with children and families, providing caregivers with daily updates.</p></li></ul><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Maintain a safe, organized and engaging therapy environment.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Qualifications:</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Registered Behavior Technician (RBT) certification — required as a condition of employment. </strong>Candidates who are not yet certified must complete ANNA's paid RBT training program (40-hour training, supervised competency assessment, and certification exam — all provided by ANNA at no cost) and obtain certification within the timeframe set by ANNA's onboarding policy. Certification must be maintained in good standing throughout employment.</p></li></ul><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Available Monday–Friday, 8:00 AM–4:30 PM.</p></li></ul><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Passionate about working with children with Autism and eager to grow in the ABA field.</p></li></ul><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong communication and interpersonal skills.</p></li></ul><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Degree in Psychology, Education, Child Development, or related field preferred (not required).</p></li></ul><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience working with children preferred.</p></li></ul><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Able to perform physically active tasks: sitting on the floor, crawling, running, lifting up to 50 lbs, and maintaining close proximity to clients during sessions.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Apply today! ANNA is an equal opportunity employer and encourages all qualified candidates to apply, even if you don't meet every requirement.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">ANNA is an equal opportunity employer. We're committed to creating a diverse, inclusive, and supportive workplace. All qualified applicants receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, national origin, age, disability, religion, sex (including pregnancy, sexual orientation, and gender identity), or any other characteristic protected by law. If you're passionate about our mission but don't meet every qualification listed, we still encourage you to apply. Your unique perspective might be exactly what we need.\"</p>","descriptionPlain":"Behavior Therapist (BT) — ABA Therapy\n\nStarting at $24–$26/hr | Full-Time | Monday–Friday, 8:00 AM–4:30 PM | No Evenings or Weekends\n\nANNA Autism Care is hiring passionate Behavior Therapists (BTs) to deliver evidence-based, 1-on-1 therapy to children with Autism using the Naturalistic Developmental Behavioral Intervention (NDBI) approach. Registered Behavior Technician (RBT) certification is a condition of employment for this role — and ANNA makes it easy: we provide the required RBT training and cover the cost of certification at no expense to you, with paid training time and extensive clinical supervision at our center-based Autism care centers across Massachusetts. \n\nWhat ANNA Autism Care Offers:\n\n - Competitive Pay + Retention Bonus: $24–$26/hr starting pay, plus a $400 retention bonus after 6 months of employment.\n\n - Comprehensive Benefits: Health, dental, and vision insurance, 401(k) with company matching, and paid time off.\n\n - Consistent Schedule: Monday–Friday, 8:00 AM–4:30 PM. No evenings, no weekends.\n\n - Full-Time Hours: 25–35 hours per week with a stable clinic-based schedule working with 5–7 clients in a clinical pod.\n\n - Free RBT Certification: ANNA provides the RBT 40-hour training, supervised competency assessment, and first certification exam attempt at no cost to you — with paid training time and a certification bonus for completing your RBT training within 2 weeks of starting.\n\n - Paid Training & Weekly Supervision: Extensive paid onboarding plus weekly clinical supervision and ongoing mentorship from BCBAs.\n\n - Career Advancement: Clear promotion paths for BTs at every stage, including BCBA sponsorship for top performers (Master's in ABA tuition covered by ANNA).\n\n - Supportive Team Culture: Monthly team lunches, seasonal celebrations, summer events, and a community that grows together.\n\nKey Responsibilities:\n\n - Implement individualized ABA therapy plans under BCBA supervision to teach new skills in communication and socialization while reducing any challenging, injurious behaviors.\n\n - Deliver play-based, child-centered therapy using the NDBI framework.\n\n - Collect accurate session data to measure each client's progress toward treatment plan goals, and communicate progress with clinical supervisors.\n\n - Assist BCBAs with assessment procedures (e.g., preference assessments and skill or behavior assessments) as directed.\n\n - Comply with applicable supervision standards, including participating in scheduled BCBA supervision and completing all required supervision and session documentation.\n\n - Obtain and maintain active Registered Behavior Technician (RBT) certification in good standing, including BACB supervision, renewal, and ethics requirements.\n\n - Build positive relationships with children and families, providing caregivers with daily updates.\n\n - Maintain a safe, organized and engaging therapy environment.\n\nQualifications:\n\n - Registered Behavior Technician (RBT) certification — required as a condition of employment. Candidates who are not yet certified must complete ANNA's paid RBT training program (40-hour training, supervised competency assessment, and certification exam — all provided by ANNA at no cost) and obtain certification within the timeframe set by ANNA's onboarding policy. Certification must be maintained in good standing throughout employment.\n\n - Available Monday–Friday, 8:00 AM–4:30 PM.\n\n - Passionate about working with children with Autism and eager to grow in the ABA field.\n\n - Strong communication and interpersonal skills.\n\n - Degree in Psychology, Education, Child Development, or related field preferred (not required).\n\n - Experience working with children preferred.\n\n - Able to perform physically active tasks: sitting on the floor, crawling, running, lifting up to 50 lbs, and maintaining close proximity to clients during sessions.\n\nApply today! ANNA is an equal opportunity employer and encourages all qualified candidates to apply, even if you don't meet every requirement.\n\nANNA is an equal opportunity employer. We're committed to creating a diverse, inclusive, and supportive workplace. All qualified applicants receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, national origin, age, disability, religion, sex (including pregnancy, sexual orientation, and gender identity), or any other characteristic protected by law. If you're passionate about our mission but don't meet every qualification listed, we still encourage you to apply. Your unique perspective might be exactly what we need.\"","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":"$24 – $26 per hour","scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[{"id":"b4c1b6d8-749f-46c6-89e1-23bb1f35eaab","tierSummary":"Billable Hourly Pay $24 – $26 per hour","title":null,"additionalInformation":null,"components":[{"id":"d5ad82e8-472b-4b4f-b446-0b61340bde83","summary":"Billable Hourly Pay $24 – $26 per hour","compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 HOUR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":24,"maxValue":26}]}],"summaryComponents":[{"compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 HOUR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":24,"maxValue":26}]}},{"id":"bdf855a8-9b5b-4d41-acde-ad27bd269c68","title":"Behavior Therapist ","department":"Clinical","team":"Behavior Therapists","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"Woburn","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":true,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-07-27T00:04:26.376+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":false,"workplaceType":"OnSite","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"Massachusetts","addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"Woburn"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/annaautismcare/bdf855a8-9b5b-4d41-acde-ad27bd269c68","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/annaautismcare/bdf855a8-9b5b-4d41-acde-ad27bd269c68/application","descriptionHtml":"<p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Behavior Therapist (BT) — ABA Therapy</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Starting at $24–$26/hr | Full-Time | Monday–Friday, 8:00 AM–4:30 PM | No Evenings or Weekends</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">ANNA Autism Care is hiring passionate Behavior Therapists (BTs) to deliver evidence-based, 1-on-1 therapy to children with Autism using the Naturalistic Developmental Behavioral Intervention (NDBI) approach. Registered Behavior Technician (RBT) certification is a condition of employment for this role — and ANNA makes it easy: we provide the required RBT training and cover the cost of certification at no expense to you, with paid training time and extensive clinical supervision at our center-based Autism care centers across Massachusetts. </p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>What ANNA Autism Care Offers:</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Competitive Pay + Retention Bonus</em>: $24–$26/hr starting pay, plus a $400 retention bonus after 6 months of employment.</p></li></ul><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Comprehensive Benefits:</em> Health, dental, and vision insurance, 401(k) with company matching, and paid time off.</p></li></ul><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Consistent Schedule:</em> Monday–Friday, 8:00 AM–4:30 PM. No evenings, no weekends.</p></li></ul><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Full-Time Hours: </em>25–35 hours per week with a stable clinic-based schedule working with 5–7 clients in a clinical pod.</p></li></ul><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Free RBT Certification:</em> ANNA provides the RBT 40-hour training, supervised competency assessment, and first certification exam attempt at no cost to you — with paid training time and a certification bonus for completing your RBT training within 2 weeks of starting.</p></li></ul><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">P<em>aid Training &amp; Weekly Supervision:</em> Extensive paid onboarding plus weekly clinical supervision and ongoing mentorship from BCBAs.</p></li></ul><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Career Advancement: </em>Clear promotion paths for BTs at every stage, including BCBA sponsorship for top performers (Master's in ABA tuition covered by ANNA).</p></li></ul><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Supportive Team Culture: </em>Monthly team lunches, seasonal celebrations, summer events, and a community that grows together.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Key Responsibilities:</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Implement individualized ABA therapy plans under BCBA supervision to teach new skills in communication and socialization while reducing any challenging, injurious behaviors.</p></li></ul><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Deliver play-based, child-centered therapy using the NDBI framework.</p></li></ul><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Collect accurate session data to measure each client's progress toward treatment plan goals, and communicate progress with clinical supervisors.</p></li></ul><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Assist BCBAs with assessment procedures (e.g., preference assessments and skill or behavior assessments) as directed.</p></li></ul><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Comply with applicable supervision standards, including participating in scheduled BCBA supervision and completing all required supervision and session documentation.</p></li></ul><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Obtain and maintain active Registered Behavior Technician (RBT) certification in good standing, including BACB supervision, renewal, and ethics requirements.</p></li></ul><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Build positive relationships with children and families, providing caregivers with daily updates.</p></li></ul><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Maintain a safe, organized and engaging therapy environment.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Qualifications:</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Registered Behavior Technician (RBT) certification — required as a condition of employment. </strong>Candidates who are not yet certified must complete ANNA's paid RBT training program (40-hour training, supervised competency assessment, and certification exam — all provided by ANNA at no cost) and obtain certification within the timeframe set by ANNA's onboarding policy. Certification must be maintained in good standing throughout employment.</p></li></ul><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Available Monday–Friday, 8:00 AM–4:30 PM.</p></li></ul><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Passionate about working with children with Autism and eager to grow in the ABA field.</p></li></ul><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong communication and interpersonal skills.</p></li></ul><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Degree in Psychology, Education, Child Development, or related field preferred (not required).</p></li></ul><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience working with children preferred.</p></li></ul><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Able to perform physically active tasks: sitting on the floor, crawling, running, lifting up to 50 lbs, and maintaining close proximity to clients during sessions.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Apply today! ANNA is an equal opportunity employer and encourages all qualified candidates to apply, even if you don't meet every requirement.</em></p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">ANNA is an equal opportunity employer. We're committed to creating a diverse, inclusive, and supportive workplace. All qualified applicants receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, national origin, age, disability, religion, sex (including pregnancy, sexual orientation, and gender identity), or any other characteristic protected by law. If you're passionate about our mission but don't meet every qualification listed, we still encourage you to apply. Your unique perspective might be exactly what we need.\"</p>","descriptionPlain":"Behavior Therapist (BT) — ABA Therapy\n\nStarting at $24–$26/hr | Full-Time | Monday–Friday, 8:00 AM–4:30 PM | No Evenings or Weekends\n\nANNA Autism Care is hiring passionate Behavior Therapists (BTs) to deliver evidence-based, 1-on-1 therapy to children with Autism using the Naturalistic Developmental Behavioral Intervention (NDBI) approach. Registered Behavior Technician (RBT) certification is a condition of employment for this role — and ANNA makes it easy: we provide the required RBT training and cover the cost of certification at no expense to you, with paid training time and extensive clinical supervision at our center-based Autism care centers across Massachusetts. \n\nWhat ANNA Autism Care Offers:\n\n - Competitive Pay + Retention Bonus: $24–$26/hr starting pay, plus a $400 retention bonus after 6 months of employment.\n\n - Comprehensive Benefits: Health, dental, and vision insurance, 401(k) with company matching, and paid time off.\n\n - Consistent Schedule: Monday–Friday, 8:00 AM–4:30 PM. No evenings, no weekends.\n\n - Full-Time Hours: 25–35 hours per week with a stable clinic-based schedule working with 5–7 clients in a clinical pod.\n\n - Free RBT Certification: ANNA provides the RBT 40-hour training, supervised competency assessment, and first certification exam attempt at no cost to you — with paid training time and a certification bonus for completing your RBT training within 2 weeks of starting.\n\n - Paid Training & Weekly Supervision: Extensive paid onboarding plus weekly clinical supervision and ongoing mentorship from BCBAs.\n\n - Career Advancement: Clear promotion paths for BTs at every stage, including BCBA sponsorship for top performers (Master's in ABA tuition covered by ANNA).\n\n - Supportive Team Culture: Monthly team lunches, seasonal celebrations, summer events, and a community that grows together.\n\nKey Responsibilities:\n\n - Implement individualized ABA therapy plans under BCBA supervision to teach new skills in communication and socialization while reducing any challenging, injurious behaviors.\n\n - Deliver play-based, child-centered therapy using the NDBI framework.\n\n - Collect accurate session data to measure each client's progress toward treatment plan goals, and communicate progress with clinical supervisors.\n\n - Assist BCBAs with assessment procedures (e.g., preference assessments and skill or behavior assessments) as directed.\n\n - Comply with applicable supervision standards, including participating in scheduled BCBA supervision and completing all required supervision and session documentation.\n\n - Obtain and maintain active Registered Behavior Technician (RBT) certification in good standing, including BACB supervision, renewal, and ethics requirements.\n\n - Build positive relationships with children and families, providing caregivers with daily updates.\n\n - Maintain a safe, organized and engaging therapy environment.\n\nQualifications:\n\n - Registered Behavior Technician (RBT) certification — required as a condition of employment. Candidates who are not yet certified must complete ANNA's paid RBT training program (40-hour training, supervised competency assessment, and certification exam — all provided by ANNA at no cost) and obtain certification within the timeframe set by ANNA's onboarding policy. Certification must be maintained in good standing throughout employment.\n\n - Available Monday–Friday, 8:00 AM–4:30 PM.\n\n - Passionate about working with children with Autism and eager to grow in the ABA field.\n\n - Strong communication and interpersonal skills.\n\n - Degree in Psychology, Education, Child Development, or related field preferred (not required).\n\n - Experience working with children preferred.\n\n - Able to perform physically active tasks: sitting on the floor, crawling, running, lifting up to 50 lbs, and maintaining close proximity to clients during sessions.\n\nApply today! ANNA is an equal opportunity employer and encourages all qualified candidates to apply, even if you don't meet every requirement.\n\n \n\nANNA is an equal opportunity employer. We're committed to creating a diverse, inclusive, and supportive workplace. All qualified applicants receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, national origin, age, disability, religion, sex (including pregnancy, sexual orientation, and gender identity), or any other characteristic protected by law. If you're passionate about our mission but don't meet every qualification listed, we still encourage you to apply. Your unique perspective might be exactly what we need.\"","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":"$24 – $26 per hour","scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[{"id":"0f45b016-834c-42a3-9f8d-58c4f64f4e5a","tierSummary":"Billable Hourly Pay $24 – $26 per hour","title":null,"additionalInformation":null,"components":[{"id":"0c64a589-cf77-469b-8e24-1d2263c8a173","summary":"Billable Hourly Pay $24 – $26 per hour","compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 HOUR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":24,"maxValue":26}]}],"summaryComponents":[{"compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 HOUR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":24,"maxValue":26}]}},{"id":"6189ee83-84f3-4b58-94ee-db9e7f7396a9","title":"Scheduling Specialist ","department":"Support Team","team":"Support Team","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"Remote - Philippines","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":true,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-05-07T18:01:41.829+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Remote","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressCountry":"Philippines"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/annaautismcare/6189ee83-84f3-4b58-94ee-db9e7f7396a9","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/annaautismcare/6189ee83-84f3-4b58-94ee-db9e7f7396a9/application","descriptionHtml":"<p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Job Title:</strong> Scheduling Specialist (Remote – Philippines Based)</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Reports to:</strong> Director of Operations</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Location:</strong> Remote (Philippines)</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Employment Type:</strong> Full-Time</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Salary</strong>: $6-$8 per hour</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Shift</strong>: 6:00 AM – 2:00 PM U.S. Eastern Time</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">6:00 PM – 2:00 AM Philippines Time during U.S. Daylight Saving Time</p></li></ul><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">7:00 PM – 3:00 AM Philippines Time during U.S. Standard Time</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Position Overview</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We're seeking a proactive and detail-oriented Scheduler to join our team and support the day-to-day creation, maintenance, and adjustment of therapy schedules across ANNA’s clinics. In this role, you will be responsible for building accurate daily and weekly schedules, responding to real‑time changes, and ensuring consistent client coverage while supporting fair staff utilization and operational guidelines.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">The Scheduler plays a critical role in coordinating schedules across multiple systems, collaborating closely with Clinical Directors and clinical team members, and ensuring schedules reflect staff availability, client needs, and clinic priorities. Success in this role requires strong attention to detail, sound judgment in fast‑changing situations, and clear, professional communication</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a fully remote position based in the Philippines. The role requires full-time availability during U.S. Eastern Time hours.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Key Responsibilities</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em><strong>Schedule Development &amp; Management</strong></em></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Create, maintain, and finalize daily and weekly clinic schedules to ensure full client coverage and appropriate staff utilization.</p></li></ul><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Build schedules using <strong>Excel </strong>and<strong> Lumary</strong>, ensuring accuracy and alignment across all systems.</p></li></ul><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Post finalized schedules within established deadlines and communicate updates promptly to clinic teams.</p></li></ul><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Anchor scheduling decisions to staff availability, client needs, and clinic operational requirements in collaboration with the Clinical Director.</p></li></ul><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Schedule observations with new BT trainees during orientation weeks.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em><strong>Respond to Changes</strong></em></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Monitor the texting dashboard in Lumary for scheduling-related messages and respond accordingly.</p></li></ul><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Respond promptly to client cancellations, late arrivals, no-shows and staff callouts by notifying team members and making necessary schedule adjustments.</p></li></ul><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Identify and implement same-day or next-day coverage solutions to minimize service disruptions</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em><strong>Staff Optimization &amp; Fair Workload Distribution</strong></em></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Balance hours across BTs, with particular attention to hourly staff equity.</p></li></ul><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Schedule staff primarily within their designated pods, ensuring cross‑pod coverage only by qualified and approved staff.</p></li></ul><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ensure compliance with required meal breaks and session duration standards.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em><strong>Non-Billable Time Oversight</strong></em></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Schedule and track non‑billable time (NBT) in alignment with weekly and daily allocation guidelines.</p></li></ul><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ensure NBT is used appropriately for approved activities (e.g., supervision, pod meetings, cleaning, observations) and approved by the Clinical Directors when necessary.</p></li></ul><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Adjust schedules strategically to maximize billable time and minimize unnecessary non‑billable hours.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Cross-Functional Collaboration</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Partner closely with Clinical Directors and clinical team members to align schedules with clinical priorities.</p></li></ul><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Participate in weekly scheduling reviews and planning meetings to prepare the upcoming week’s schedule.</p></li></ul><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Incorporate team and client updates shared by clinical staff into schedules in a timely and consistent manner.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Qualifications</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Prior experience in scheduling, staffing coordination, or healthcare operations (especially ABA or allied health) preferred</p></li></ul><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong English communication skills, both written and verbal</p></li></ul><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Exceptional attention to detail and ability to manage shifting priorities quickly</p></li></ul><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Proficient with scheduling software, spreadsheets (Google Sheets/Excel), and time zone coordination</p></li></ul><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Comfortable working independently and during work hours noted above.</p></li></ul><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Reliable internet connection and quiet work environment</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Why Join ANNA?</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Help shape the future of autism care for children and families</p></li></ul><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Be part of a mission-driven, supportive, and growth-oriented team</p></li></ul><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Work remotely with a flexible, international operations team</p></li></ul><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Competitive compensation with growth potential</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">ANNA is an equal opportunity employer. We're committed to creating a diverse, inclusive, and supportive workplace. All qualified applicants receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, national origin, age, disability, religion, sex (including pregnancy, sexual orientation, and gender identity), or any other characteristic protected by law. If you're passionate about our mission but don't meet every qualification listed, we still encourage you to apply. Your unique perspective might be exactly what we need.\"</p>","descriptionPlain":"Job Title: Scheduling Specialist (Remote – Philippines Based)\n\nReports to: Director of Operations\n\nLocation: Remote (Philippines)\n\nEmployment Type: Full-Time\n\nSalary: $6-$8 per hour\n\nShift: 6:00 AM – 2:00 PM U.S. Eastern Time\n\n - 6:00 PM – 2:00 AM Philippines Time during U.S. Daylight Saving Time\n\n - 7:00 PM – 3:00 AM Philippines Time during U.S. Standard Time\n\nPosition Overview\n\nWe're seeking a proactive and detail-oriented Scheduler to join our team and support the day-to-day creation, maintenance, and adjustment of therapy schedules across ANNA’s clinics. In this role, you will be responsible for building accurate daily and weekly schedules, responding to real‑time changes, and ensuring consistent client coverage while supporting fair staff utilization and operational guidelines.\n\nThe Scheduler plays a critical role in coordinating schedules across multiple systems, collaborating closely with Clinical Directors and clinical team members, and ensuring schedules reflect staff availability, client needs, and clinic priorities. Success in this role requires strong attention to detail, sound judgment in fast‑changing situations, and clear, professional communication\n\nThis is a fully remote position based in the Philippines. The role requires full-time availability during U.S. Eastern Time hours.\n\n\n\nKey Responsibilities\n\nSchedule Development & Management\n\n - Create, maintain, and finalize daily and weekly clinic schedules to ensure full client coverage and appropriate staff utilization.\n\n - Build schedules using Excel and Lumary, ensuring accuracy and alignment across all systems.\n\n - Post finalized schedules within established deadlines and communicate updates promptly to clinic teams.\n\n - Anchor scheduling decisions to staff availability, client needs, and clinic operational requirements in collaboration with the Clinical Director.\n\n - Schedule observations with new BT trainees during orientation weeks.\n\nRespond to Changes\n\n - Monitor the texting dashboard in Lumary for scheduling-related messages and respond accordingly.\n\n - Respond promptly to client cancellations, late arrivals, no-shows and staff callouts by notifying team members and making necessary schedule adjustments.\n\n - Identify and implement same-day or next-day coverage solutions to minimize service disruptions\n\nStaff Optimization & Fair Workload Distribution\n\n - Balance hours across BTs, with particular attention to hourly staff equity.\n\n - Schedule staff primarily within their designated pods, ensuring cross‑pod coverage only by qualified and approved staff.\n\n - Ensure compliance with required meal breaks and session duration standards.\n\nNon-Billable Time Oversight\n\n - Schedule and track non‑billable time (NBT) in alignment with weekly and daily allocation guidelines.\n\n - Ensure NBT is used appropriately for approved activities (e.g., supervision, pod meetings, cleaning, observations) and approved by the Clinical Directors when necessary.\n\n - Adjust schedules strategically to maximize billable time and minimize unnecessary non‑billable hours.\n\nCross-Functional Collaboration\n\n - Partner closely with Clinical Directors and clinical team members to align schedules with clinical priorities.\n\n - Participate in weekly scheduling reviews and planning meetings to prepare the upcoming week’s schedule.\n\n - Incorporate team and client updates shared by clinical staff into schedules in a timely and consistent manner.\n   \n   \n\nQualifications\n\n - Prior experience in scheduling, staffing coordination, or healthcare operations (especially ABA or allied health) preferred\n\n - Strong English communication skills, both written and verbal\n\n - Exceptional attention to detail and ability to manage shifting priorities quickly\n\n - Proficient with scheduling software, spreadsheets (Google Sheets/Excel), and time zone coordination\n\n - Comfortable working independently and during work hours noted above.\n\n - Reliable internet connection and quiet work environment\n\nWhy Join ANNA?\n\n - Help shape the future of autism care for children and families\n\n - Be part of a mission-driven, supportive, and growth-oriented team\n\n - Work remotely with a flexible, international operations team\n\n - Competitive compensation with growth potential\n\nANNA is an equal opportunity employer. We're committed to creating a diverse, inclusive, and supportive workplace. All qualified applicants receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, national origin, age, disability, religion, sex (including pregnancy, sexual orientation, and gender identity), or any other characteristic protected by law. If you're passionate about our mission but don't meet every qualification listed, we still encourage you to apply. Your unique perspective might be exactly what we need.\"","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":"$12,480 – $16,640","scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":"$12,480 - $16,640","compensationTiers":[{"id":"c87652d5-3f82-4469-affe-f72767660b37","tierSummary":"Base Salary $12,480 – $16,640","title":null,"additionalInformation":null,"components":[{"id":"285ec469-48a0-40d8-8e15-47dd85122a46","summary":"Base Salary $12,480 – $16,640","compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":12480,"maxValue":16640}]}],"summaryComponents":[{"compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":12480,"maxValue":16640}]}},{"id":"bdef21ba-613b-4900-ad17-0957adec5edb","title":"Market Launch & Operations Project Manager","department":"Support Team","team":"Operations","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"Remote - Philippines","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":true,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-06-24T04:15:05.712+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Remote","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressCountry":"Philippines"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/annaautismcare/bdef21ba-613b-4900-ad17-0957adec5edb","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/annaautismcare/bdef21ba-613b-4900-ad17-0957adec5edb/application","descriptionHtml":"<p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>ANNA Autism Care</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Market Launch &amp; Operations Project Manager</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Remote (Philippines) | Full-time, US Eastern Hours</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">$24,000 – $36,000 USD (~₱1,400,000 – ₱2,220,000 PHP) annually, commensurate with experience</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>About ANNA</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">ANNA (Allied Network for Neurodevelopmental Advancement) is a high-growth, US-based startup providing ABA services to young autistic children (under age 6) and their families using a neurodiversity-affirming, Naturalistic Developmental Behavioral Intervention (NDBI) approach. We operate centers across Massachusetts and are scaling into new markets fast, both through acquisitions and through new centers we build from scratch. We are building the operational backbone of a modern autism care company from the ground up, and we want operators on the team who are excited to build it with us.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Position Overview</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">The Market Launch &amp; Operations Project Manager is the execution engine behind ANNA’s expansion into new markets, and a project-management-forward right hand for the CEO. You will partner closely with the Implementation Director who owns a market’s full P&amp;L and operations, serving as their execution arm: running the tactical work that gets a new center open and a new market live, then supporting the operations that keep it running. Markets come online two ways at ANNA, through acquisition and through de novo center builds, and you will help with both, plus the steady-state operations of markets once they are up.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This role is built around three things. First, project management: you will run multiple concurrent workstreams, hold the plan, manage dependencies and risks, and keep cross-functional partners moving. Second, new-market launch and operations: from hiring the first clinicians and getting the first center physically open, to rounding out the contracts and systems a market needs, to integrating an acquired clinic, to supporting the Implementation Director on the day-to-day running of the market. Third, a broad bucket of operations and executive leverage: the ambiguous, time-bounded, “can you figure this out by Friday” work that does not fit neatly into any one department, plus making sure the things that matter to the CEO actually get done.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">What makes this role different is the explicit expectation of AI fluency. You will be a heavy daily user of Claude: building automations, Projects, and Cowork workspaces, stitching tools together via MCP, and turning repetitive execution work into reliable, documented workflows. The right hire treats AI tooling not as a novelty but as a force multiplier they reach for first. You will work full-time on US Eastern hours from the Philippines, partnering primarily with the Implementation Director and directly with the CEO and broader leadership team in Boston.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Compensation &amp; Engagement</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Base Salary</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">$24,000 – $36,000 USD (~₱1,400,000 – ₱2,220,000 PHP) annually, commensurate with experience</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Schedule</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Full-time, US Eastern Time business hours (approx. 9pm – 6am Manila)</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Time Off</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Flexible PTO; US holidays observed</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What You’ll Do</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Project Management &amp; Delivery</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">• Own project plans, timelines, and trackers across multiple concurrent workstreams, holding the single source of truth on what is happening, who owns it, and when it is due</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">• Run the operating cadence that keeps work moving: status updates, check-ins, risk flags, and dependency management, so nothing stalls quietly</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">• Keep cross-functional projects coordinated and unblocked across Clinical Operations, Finance, IT, People Operations, and external vendors</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">• Build repeatable playbooks for recurring project types (new-market launch, center buildout, clinic integration, vendor onboarding) so each one runs faster and cleaner than the last</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">• Be the person leadership trusts with ambiguous, time-bounded asks: the kind of project where someone says “can you figure this out by Friday” and it actually gets figured out</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>New-Market Launch &amp; Market Operations</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">• Serve as the execution arm for the Implementation Director who owns a market’s P&amp;L and operations: turn their priorities into tracked workstreams and drive the tactical work to done</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">• Help bring the first center in a new market online by coordinating real estate and buildout operations: landlord and contractor coordination, permits and occupancy, furniture and equipment procurement, signage, IT, phones, internet, and supplies, so the center is ready for kids on schedule</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">• Support hiring the first clinicians and clinic leadership in a new market: post roles, coordinate interview scheduling and candidate communications, manage offer logistics, and run a clean onboarding, including license and credentialing setup</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">• Round out the contracts and vendor agreements a new market needs but does not yet have in place, and keep them organized, tracked, and renewed</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">• For acquisitions, own the integration mechanics: EMR migration, HRIS and ATS setup, Microsoft 365 and email provisioning, credentialing and payer transitions, state-specific compliance filings, and harmonizing the acquired team’s policies and SOPs to ANNA’s</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">• Support the ongoing operations of live markets: keep licensing and credentialing current, manage vendor and contract renewals, track operational metrics, and chase the long tail of recurring items so nothing slips through the cracks</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>The Broad Bucket of Operations</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">• Take on operational projects that do not yet have a clear owner: vendor onboarding and license tracking, internal comms support, document and SOP cleanup, ad-hoc research, and similar connective-tissue work that keeps a fast-growing, multi-state company running</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">• Partner with Clinical Operations, Finance, IT, and external vendors so operational processes plug cleanly into adjacent systems and do not create downstream rework</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">• Pull together clean research, analysis, and options when leadership needs a decision supported quickly</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Executive Leverage (Right Hand to the CEO)</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">• Translate the CEO’s priorities into tracked, driven workstreams with clear owners, dates, and status, then own the follow-through until they close</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">• Prep the CEO and the Implementation Director for the week and key meetings: pre-reads pulled together, materials in the right place at the right time, action items captured and chased to done</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">• Build the trackers, dashboards, and lightweight reporting that let leadership see status at a glance instead of asking</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">• Provide light coordination and scheduling support on the projects you own, with the judgment to know what to handle, what to surface, and what to deflect</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>AI-Native Workflow Building</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">• Use Claude daily as your primary thinking, drafting, and execution partner: project plans, status updates, research, summaries, comms, and data cleanup</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">• Build Claude Projects, Cowork workspaces, and reusable prompts and skills that codify how recurring execution work gets done at ANNA: launch playbooks, center-opening checklists, integration playbooks, vendor tracking, and project reporting</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">• Identify manual or repetitive steps in our processes and replace them with well-scoped automations using Claude, MCP servers, Asana, SharePoint, and our other systems</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">• Document every workflow you build so anyone on the team can run it; treat the workflow library as a product you own and improve over time</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Qualifications</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Required</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">• 3+ years in project management, program coordination, business operations, operations, or chief-of-staff and PMO-style support at a fast-paced company</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">• Demonstrated ability to run multiple concurrent projects to deadline with minimal oversight, with strong organizational and tracking discipline</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">• Comfort coordinating logistics across many stakeholders at once (vendors, contractors, hiring managers, internal teams) and keeping all of it moving</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">• Strong daily, hands-on use of generative AI tools (Claude preferred; ChatGPT, Gemini, Copilot acceptable) beyond casual use; you can talk concretely about workflows you have built</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">• Excellent written English; clean, warm, professional communication on email, Slack, and async docs</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">• Proven ability to work full-time US Eastern hours (approx. 9pm – 6am Philippine Time) and a stable, reliable home work setup</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">• High standard for accuracy and discretion; you treat sensitive company, employee, and transaction data with appropriate care</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Preferred</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">• Fluency with at least one major project management tool (Asana strongly preferred; Monday, Jira, Smartsheet, ClickUp acceptable), and familiarity with an ATS and/or HRIS</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">• Experience launching new sites or markets, M&amp;A integration, or multi-site and multi-state operations</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">• Experience coordinating real estate buildouts, facilities, or high-volume hiring and onboarding</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">• Experience supporting US-based startups or scale-ups from the Philippines</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">• Experience in healthcare, behavioral health, or another regulated industry</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">• Familiarity with MCP servers, Claude Projects, Cowork, and stitching AI tools to systems like Asana, SharePoint, Microsoft 365, or Salesforce</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">• Experience in a high-growth or scaling startup environment</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">• Comfort with light SQL, spreadsheet formulas, or no-code automation tools (Zapier, Make, Airtable automations)</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">• Experience drafting or maintaining operational SOPs, playbooks, or process documentation</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>If you don’t meet every preferred qualification, we still encourage you to apply.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Ideal Candidate</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You are a meticulous, mission-driven operator who thrives in fast-moving environments where the rules are still being written. You are equally happy holding a launch tracker for a brand-new center, chasing a contractor to keep an opening on schedule, posting the first clinician roles in a new market, prepping the CEO for a board call, and shipping a Claude workflow that compresses a four-hour task into ten minutes. You take pride in being the person who never drops a ball, who anticipates the next thing before being asked, and who leaves every process they touch better than they found it. You are energized, not unsettled, by AI, and you see the opportunity to be one of the most leveraged operations hires in the country because of how you use it.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Our Commitment to Inclusion</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">ANNA is an equal opportunity employer. We celebrate diversity and are committed to an inclusive environment where all team members can thrive. We welcome candidates of all backgrounds and experiences.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Why ANNA?</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At ANNA, we are working to transform autism care by combining rigorous clinical training, compassionate family-centered practice, and neurodiversity-affirming approaches. Our NDBI model supports each child’s strengths through play-based, developmentally informed care. This role is how we make sure that every time ANNA enters a new market, whether by opening a new center or absorbing an existing one, it comes online cleanly and runs well, so the operators and clinicians delivering that care can focus on kids and families.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Learn more about us: <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://annaautismcare.com/about-us/\">https://annaautismcare.com/about-us/</a></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Remote, Philippines-based, full-time US Eastern hours.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">ANNA is an equal opportunity employer. We're committed to creating a diverse, inclusive, and supportive workplace. All qualified applicants receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, national origin, age, disability, religion, sex (including pregnancy, sexual orientation, and gender identity), or any other characteristic protected by law. If you're passionate about our mission but don't meet every qualification listed, we still encourage you to apply. Your unique perspective might be exactly what we need.\"</p>","descriptionPlain":"ANNA Autism Care\n\nMarket Launch & Operations Project Manager\n\nRemote (Philippines) | Full-time, US Eastern Hours\n\n$24,000 – $36,000 USD (~₱1,400,000 – ₱2,220,000 PHP) annually, commensurate with experience\n\n\n\n\nABOUT ANNA\n\nANNA (Allied Network for Neurodevelopmental Advancement) is a high-growth, US-based startup providing ABA services to young autistic children (under age 6) and their families using a neurodiversity-affirming, Naturalistic Developmental Behavioral Intervention (NDBI) approach. We operate centers across Massachusetts and are scaling into new markets fast, both through acquisitions and through new centers we build from scratch. We are building the operational backbone of a modern autism care company from the ground up, and we want operators on the team who are excited to build it with us.\n\n\n\n\nPOSITION OVERVIEW\n\nThe Market Launch & Operations Project Manager is the execution engine behind ANNA’s expansion into new markets, and a project-management-forward right hand for the CEO. You will partner closely with the Implementation Director who owns a market’s full P&L and operations, serving as their execution arm: running the tactical work that gets a new center open and a new market live, then supporting the operations that keep it running. Markets come online two ways at ANNA, through acquisition and through de novo center builds, and you will help with both, plus the steady-state operations of markets once they are up.\n\nThis role is built around three things. First, project management: you will run multiple concurrent workstreams, hold the plan, manage dependencies and risks, and keep cross-functional partners moving. Second, new-market launch and operations: from hiring the first clinicians and getting the first center physically open, to rounding out the contracts and systems a market needs, to integrating an acquired clinic, to supporting the Implementation Director on the day-to-day running of the market. Third, a broad bucket of operations and executive leverage: the ambiguous, time-bounded, “can you figure this out by Friday” work that does not fit neatly into any one department, plus making sure the things that matter to the CEO actually get done.\n\nWhat makes this role different is the explicit expectation of AI fluency. You will be a heavy daily user of Claude: building automations, Projects, and Cowork workspaces, stitching tools together via MCP, and turning repetitive execution work into reliable, documented workflows. The right hire treats AI tooling not as a novelty but as a force multiplier they reach for first. You will work full-time on US Eastern hours from the Philippines, partnering primarily with the Implementation Director and directly with the CEO and broader leadership team in Boston.\n\n\n\n\nCOMPENSATION & ENGAGEMENT\n\nBase Salary\n\n$24,000 – $36,000 USD (~₱1,400,000 – ₱2,220,000 PHP) annually, commensurate with experience\n\nSchedule\n\nFull-time, US Eastern Time business hours (approx. 9pm – 6am Manila)\n\nTime Off\n\nFlexible PTO; US holidays observed\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU’LL DO\n\nProject Management & Delivery\n\n• Own project plans, timelines, and trackers across multiple concurrent workstreams, holding the single source of truth on what is happening, who owns it, and when it is due\n\n• Run the operating cadence that keeps work moving: status updates, check-ins, risk flags, and dependency management, so nothing stalls quietly\n\n• Keep cross-functional projects coordinated and unblocked across Clinical Operations, Finance, IT, People Operations, and external vendors\n\n• Build repeatable playbooks for recurring project types (new-market launch, center buildout, clinic integration, vendor onboarding) so each one runs faster and cleaner than the last\n\n• Be the person leadership trusts with ambiguous, time-bounded asks: the kind of project where someone says “can you figure this out by Friday” and it actually gets figured out\n\n\n\nNew-Market Launch & Market Operations\n\n• Serve as the execution arm for the Implementation Director who owns a market’s P&L and operations: turn their priorities into tracked workstreams and drive the tactical work to done\n\n• Help bring the first center in a new market online by coordinating real estate and buildout operations: landlord and contractor coordination, permits and occupancy, furniture and equipment procurement, signage, IT, phones, internet, and supplies, so the center is ready for kids on schedule\n\n• Support hiring the first clinicians and clinic leadership in a new market: post roles, coordinate interview scheduling and candidate communications, manage offer logistics, and run a clean onboarding, including license and credentialing setup\n\n• Round out the contracts and vendor agreements a new market needs but does not yet have in place, and keep them organized, tracked, and renewed\n\n• For acquisitions, own the integration mechanics: EMR migration, HRIS and ATS setup, Microsoft 365 and email provisioning, credentialing and payer transitions, state-specific compliance filings, and harmonizing the acquired team’s policies and SOPs to ANNA’s\n\n• Support the ongoing operations of live markets: keep licensing and credentialing current, manage vendor and contract renewals, track operational metrics, and chase the long tail of recurring items so nothing slips through the cracks\n\n\n\nThe Broad Bucket of Operations\n\n• Take on operational projects that do not yet have a clear owner: vendor onboarding and license tracking, internal comms support, document and SOP cleanup, ad-hoc research, and similar connective-tissue work that keeps a fast-growing, multi-state company running\n\n• Partner with Clinical Operations, Finance, IT, and external vendors so operational processes plug cleanly into adjacent systems and do not create downstream rework\n\n• Pull together clean research, analysis, and options when leadership needs a decision supported quickly\n\n\n\nExecutive Leverage (Right Hand to the CEO)\n\n• Translate the CEO’s priorities into tracked, driven workstreams with clear owners, dates, and status, then own the follow-through until they close\n\n• Prep the CEO and the Implementation Director for the week and key meetings: pre-reads pulled together, materials in the right place at the right time, action items captured and chased to done\n\n• Build the trackers, dashboards, and lightweight reporting that let leadership see status at a glance instead of asking\n\n• Provide light coordination and scheduling support on the projects you own, with the judgment to know what to handle, what to surface, and what to deflect\n\n\n\nAI-Native Workflow Building\n\n• Use Claude daily as your primary thinking, drafting, and execution partner: project plans, status updates, research, summaries, comms, and data cleanup\n\n• Build Claude Projects, Cowork workspaces, and reusable prompts and skills that codify how recurring execution work gets done at ANNA: launch playbooks, center-opening checklists, integration playbooks, vendor tracking, and project reporting\n\n• Identify manual or repetitive steps in our processes and replace them with well-scoped automations using Claude, MCP servers, Asana, SharePoint, and our other systems\n\n• Document every workflow you build so anyone on the team can run it; treat the workflow library as a product you own and improve over time\n\n\n\n\nQUALIFICATIONS\n\nRequired\n\n• 3+ years in project management, program coordination, business operations, operations, or chief-of-staff and PMO-style support at a fast-paced company\n\n• Demonstrated ability to run multiple concurrent projects to deadline with minimal oversight, with strong organizational and tracking discipline\n\n• Comfort coordinating logistics across many stakeholders at once (vendors, contractors, hiring managers, internal teams) and keeping all of it moving\n\n• Strong daily, hands-on use of generative AI tools (Claude preferred; ChatGPT, Gemini, Copilot acceptable) beyond casual use; you can talk concretely about workflows you have built\n\n• Excellent written English; clean, warm, professional communication on email, Slack, and async docs\n\n• Proven ability to work full-time US Eastern hours (approx. 9pm – 6am Philippine Time) and a stable, reliable home work setup\n\n• High standard for accuracy and discretion; you treat sensitive company, employee, and transaction data with appropriate care\n\nPreferred\n\n• Fluency with at least one major project management tool (Asana strongly preferred; Monday, Jira, Smartsheet, ClickUp acceptable), and familiarity with an ATS and/or HRIS\n\n• Experience launching new sites or markets, M&A integration, or multi-site and multi-state operations\n\n• Experience coordinating real estate buildouts, facilities, or high-volume hiring and onboarding\n\n• Experience supporting US-based startups or scale-ups from the Philippines\n\n• Experience in healthcare, behavioral health, or another regulated industry\n\n• Familiarity with MCP servers, Claude Projects, Cowork, and stitching AI tools to systems like Asana, SharePoint, Microsoft 365, or Salesforce\n\n• Experience in a high-growth or scaling startup environment\n\n• Comfort with light SQL, spreadsheet formulas, or no-code automation tools (Zapier, Make, Airtable automations)\n\n• Experience drafting or maintaining operational SOPs, playbooks, or process documentation\n\nIf you don’t meet every preferred qualification, we still encourage you to apply.\n\n\n\n\nIDEAL CANDIDATE\n\nYou are a meticulous, mission-driven operator who thrives in fast-moving environments where the rules are still being written. You are equally happy holding a launch tracker for a brand-new center, chasing a contractor to keep an opening on schedule, posting the first clinician roles in a new market, prepping the CEO for a board call, and shipping a Claude workflow that compresses a four-hour task into ten minutes. You take pride in being the person who never drops a ball, who anticipates the next thing before being asked, and who leaves every process they touch better than they found it. You are energized, not unsettled, by AI, and you see the opportunity to be one of the most leveraged operations hires in the country because of how you use it.\n\n\n\nOur Commitment to Inclusion\n\nANNA is an equal opportunity employer. We celebrate diversity and are committed to an inclusive environment where all team members can thrive. We welcome candidates of all backgrounds and experiences.\n\n\n\nWhy ANNA?\n\nAt ANNA, we are working to transform autism care by combining rigorous clinical training, compassionate family-centered practice, and neurodiversity-affirming approaches. Our NDBI model supports each child’s strengths through play-based, developmentally informed care. This role is how we make sure that every time ANNA enters a new market, whether by opening a new center or absorbing an existing one, it comes online cleanly and runs well, so the operators and clinicians delivering that care can focus on kids and families.\n\nLearn more about us: https://annaautismcare.com/about-us/\n\nRemote, Philippines-based, full-time US Eastern hours.\n\nANNA is an equal opportunity employer. We're committed to creating a diverse, inclusive, and supportive workplace. All qualified applicants receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, national origin, age, disability, religion, sex (including pregnancy, sexual orientation, and gender identity), or any other characteristic protected by law. If you're passionate about our mission but don't meet every qualification listed, we still encourage you to apply. Your unique perspective might be exactly what we need.\"","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":"$24K – $38K","scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":"$24K - $38K","compensationTiers":[{"id":"63a3138e-e1a4-4339-a194-ff6ddadb28a0","tierSummary":"$24K – $38K","title":null,"additionalInformation":null,"components":[{"id":"168dccca-4d25-45ae-a0e6-fd327ce86eed","summary":"$24K – $38K","compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":24000,"maxValue":38000}]}],"summaryComponents":[{"compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":24000,"maxValue":38000}]}},{"id":"ebd19951-9899-416a-915e-ef7961cdcc1d","title":"Business Operations Specialist","department":"Support Team","team":"Operations","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"Remote - Philippines","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":true,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-07-15T11:42:20.623+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Remote","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressCountry":"Philippines"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/annaautismcare/ebd19951-9899-416a-915e-ef7961cdcc1d","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/annaautismcare/ebd19951-9899-416a-915e-ef7961cdcc1d/application","descriptionHtml":"<h1><strong>ANNA Autism Care</strong></h1><h2><strong>Business Operations Specialist</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Remote (Philippines) | Full-time, US Eastern Hours</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">$24,000 – $36,000 USD (~₱1,400,000 – ₱2,220,000 PHP) </p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><h1>About ANNA</h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">ANNA (Allied Network for Neurodevelopmental Advancement) is a mission-driven organization that provides ABA services to young autistic children (under the age of 6) and their families using a neurodiversity-affirming, Naturalistic Developmental Behavioral Intervention (NDBI) approach. We operate center-based clinics across Massachusetts and Missouri and are growing quickly — and we're looking for a versatile, AI-fluent Business Operations Specialist to help us build the operational backbone of a fast-scaling, multi-state organization.</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><h1>Position Overview</h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">The Business Operations Specialist is a generalist operator role at the center of ANNA's business operations. Based in the Philippines and working full-time US Eastern Time hours, you'll take ownership of the cross-functional operational work that keeps a fast-growing, multi-state healthcare organization running — from vendor and contractor management to financial operations support, clinic operations coordination, market launch support, data and reporting, and a rotating portfolio of special projects.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">What makes this role distinctive: we're looking for someone who is genuinely fluent with modern AI tools — particularly Claude — and uses them every day to multiply their own output. You won't just complete tasks; you'll build the Projects, automations, and Cowork workflows that make every future iteration of similar work faster and better.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This role reports directly to our Co-Founder &amp; CEO and partners closely with US-based Operations, Finance, People, and Clinical leadership teams.</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><h1>Compensation &amp; Engagement</h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Base Salary</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">$24,000 – $36,000 USD (~₱1,400,000 – ₱2,220,000 PHP) </p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Time Off</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Flexible PTO and paid US holidays</p></li></ul><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><h1>What You'll Do</h1><h2><em><strong>Business Operations &amp; Project Execution</strong></em></h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Own a rotating portfolio of cross-functional operational projects end-to-end — scoping, execution, stakeholder communication, and documentation</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Manage vendor and contractor relationships: sourcing, onboarding, invoice tracking, renewals, and performance follow-up</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Support financial operations in partnership with our finance function: AP workflows, expense policy compliance, reconciliation support, and month-end coordination</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Coordinate operational support for our clinics across Massachusetts and Missouri — supplies, facilities follow-ups, licensing and credentialing tracking, and center-opening logistics support</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Build and maintain SOPs so that every process you touch is documented, repeatable, and improvable</p></li></ul><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><h2><em><strong>Market Launch &amp; Expansion Support</strong></em></h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Support new-market launches — both de novo center openings and acquisition integrations — including launch checklist ownership, vendor and licensing coordination, and timeline tracking</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Drive system migrations and integrations for acquired entities, partnering with Finance and People on cutover planning and data integrity</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Build and maintain our reusable launch playbook so each successive market opening is faster and cleaner than the last</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Coordinate cross-functional launch workstreams across Operations, Clinical, Finance, and People, keeping owners accountable to dates</p></li></ul><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><h2><em><strong>Systems, Data &amp; Reporting</strong></em></h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Administer and maintain our operational systems (Rippling, Ramp, internal trackers), keeping data clean, current, and trustworthy</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Build and maintain recurring operational reporting — weekly dashboards, KPI rollups, and ad hoc analyses for leadership</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Audit data quality across systems on a recurring cadence and drive fixes at the source, not just the symptom</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Serve as the connective tissue between systems — when data lives in three places, you make sure it agrees</p></li></ul><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><h2><em><strong>AI-Powered Automation &amp; Tooling</strong></em></h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Use Claude (Projects, Cowork, Claude Code) to build automations and workflows that eliminate manual work across business operations</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Maintain a library of internal Claude Projects the broader ANNA team can use (report builders, vendor comparison tools, SOP generators, data-cleanup workflows)</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Identify high-friction processes and propose AI-assisted improvements before being asked</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Stay current on AI tooling and bring new ideas to the team</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div></li></ul><h2><em><strong>Cross-functional Partnership</strong></em></h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Work closely with US-based Operations, Finance, People, and Clinical leadership teams — async-by-default, with anchor sync hours during EST overlap</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Communicate clearly and proactively across time zones, with strong written status updates</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Escalate appropriately and exercise judgment in ambiguity</p></li></ul><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><h1>Qualifications</h1><h2><em>Required</em></h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">3+ years in business operations, operations, consulting, finance operations, or a similar generalist role</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Demonstrated ability to work full-time US Eastern Time hours (approx. 9 PM – 6 AM Manila time, including DST shifts)</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Hands-on experience with modern business systems (e.g., Ramp/<a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"http://Bill.com\">Bill.com</a>, Rippling or similar HRIS, QuickBooks exposure a plus)</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Demonstrated AI fluency — must be able to show actual work product (Claude Projects, automations, prompt engineering, agent workflows, or similar). Curiosity is not enough; we want to see what you've built.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Excellent written English and async communication skills</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong organizational judgment — able to prioritize, own, and finish work without close supervision</p></li></ul><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><h2><em>Preferred</em></h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience supporting US-based healthcare, multi-site, or services organizations</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience supporting new site openings, M&amp;A integration, or market expansion</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience in a startup or high-growth environment</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Exposure to financial operations (AP, reconciliation, expense management)</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience building dashboards or operational reporting</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>If you don't meet every preferred qualification, we still encourage you to apply.</em></p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><h1>Ideal Candidate</h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You are a systems-minded operator who thrives in fast-moving, ambiguous environments. You are a builder at heart — comfortable owning cross-functional projects end-to-end, keeping operational data trustworthy, and turning messy processes into clean, documented systems. You balance meticulous execution with genuine creativity about how AI can multiply your output, and you're energized by the idea that the automations you build become permanent infrastructure for a growing organization. You are motivated by an opportunity to be an early, high-leverage operational hire at a mission-driven company transforming autism care across multiple states.</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><h1>Why ANNA?</h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At ANNA, we are working to transform autism care by combining rigorous clinical training, compassionate family-centered practice, and neurodiversity-affirming approaches. Our Naturalistic Developmental Behavioral Intervention (NDBI) model supports each child's strengths through play-based, developmentally informed care.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">As our Business Operations Specialist, you'll build the operational infrastructure that lets our clinical teams focus on what matters most — delivering exceptional care to children and families.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You can learn more about us here: <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://annaautismcare.com/about-us/\">https://annaautismcare.com/about-us/</a></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Location:</strong><em> Remote, Philippines-based, full-time US Eastern hours.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>ANNA Autism Care | Business Operations Specialist</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">ANNA is an equal opportunity employer. We're committed to creating a diverse, inclusive, and supportive workplace. All qualified applicants receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, national origin, age, disability, religion, sex (including pregnancy, sexual orientation, and gender identity), or any other characteristic protected by law. If you're passionate about our mission but don't meet every qualification listed, we still encourage you to apply. Your unique perspective might be exactly what we need.\"</p>","descriptionPlain":"ANNA AUTISM CARE\n\n\nBUSINESS OPERATIONS SPECIALIST\n\nRemote (Philippines) | Full-time, US Eastern Hours\n\n$24,000 – $36,000 USD (~₱1,400,000 – ₱2,220,000 PHP) \n\n \n\n\nABOUT ANNA\n\nANNA (Allied Network for Neurodevelopmental Advancement) is a mission-driven organization that provides ABA services to young autistic children (under the age of 6) and their families using a neurodiversity-affirming, Naturalistic Developmental Behavioral Intervention (NDBI) approach. We operate center-based clinics across Massachusetts and Missouri and are growing quickly — and we're looking for a versatile, AI-fluent Business Operations Specialist to help us build the operational backbone of a fast-scaling, multi-state organization.\n\n \n\n\nPOSITION OVERVIEW\n\nThe Business Operations Specialist is a generalist operator role at the center of ANNA's business operations. Based in the Philippines and working full-time US Eastern Time hours, you'll take ownership of the cross-functional operational work that keeps a fast-growing, multi-state healthcare organization running — from vendor and contractor management to financial operations support, clinic operations coordination, market launch support, data and reporting, and a rotating portfolio of special projects.\n\nWhat makes this role distinctive: we're looking for someone who is genuinely fluent with modern AI tools — particularly Claude — and uses them every day to multiply their own output. You won't just complete tasks; you'll build the Projects, automations, and Cowork workflows that make every future iteration of similar work faster and better.\n\nThis role reports directly to our Co-Founder & CEO and partners closely with US-based Operations, Finance, People, and Clinical leadership teams.\n\n \n \n\n\nCOMPENSATION & ENGAGEMENT\n\nBase Salary\n\n - $24,000 – $36,000 USD (~₱1,400,000 – ₱2,220,000 PHP) \n\nTime Off\n\n - Flexible PTO and paid US holidays\n\n \n\n\nWHAT YOU'LL DO\n\n\nBUSINESS OPERATIONS & PROJECT EXECUTION\n\n - Own a rotating portfolio of cross-functional operational projects end-to-end — scoping, execution, stakeholder communication, and documentation\n\n - Manage vendor and contractor relationships: sourcing, onboarding, invoice tracking, renewals, and performance follow-up\n\n - Support financial operations in partnership with our finance function: AP workflows, expense policy compliance, reconciliation support, and month-end coordination\n\n - Coordinate operational support for our clinics across Massachusetts and Missouri — supplies, facilities follow-ups, licensing and credentialing tracking, and center-opening logistics support\n\n - Build and maintain SOPs so that every process you touch is documented, repeatable, and improvable\n\n \n\n\nMARKET LAUNCH & EXPANSION SUPPORT\n\n - Support new-market launches — both de novo center openings and acquisition integrations — including launch checklist ownership, vendor and licensing coordination, and timeline tracking\n\n - Drive system migrations and integrations for acquired entities, partnering with Finance and People on cutover planning and data integrity\n\n - Build and maintain our reusable launch playbook so each successive market opening is faster and cleaner than the last\n\n - Coordinate cross-functional launch workstreams across Operations, Clinical, Finance, and People, keeping owners accountable to dates\n\n \n\n\nSYSTEMS, DATA & REPORTING\n\n - Administer and maintain our operational systems (Rippling, Ramp, internal trackers), keeping data clean, current, and trustworthy\n\n - Build and maintain recurring operational reporting — weekly dashboards, KPI rollups, and ad hoc analyses for leadership\n\n - Audit data quality across systems on a recurring cadence and drive fixes at the source, not just the symptom\n\n - Serve as the connective tissue between systems — when data lives in three places, you make sure it agrees\n\n \n\n\nAI-POWERED AUTOMATION & TOOLING\n\n - Use Claude (Projects, Cowork, Claude Code) to build automations and workflows that eliminate manual work across business operations\n\n - Maintain a library of internal Claude Projects the broader ANNA team can use (report builders, vendor comparison tools, SOP generators, data-cleanup workflows)\n\n - Identify high-friction processes and propose AI-assisted improvements before being asked\n\n - Stay current on AI tooling and bring new ideas to the team\n   \n    \n\n\nCROSS-FUNCTIONAL PARTNERSHIP\n\n - Work closely with US-based Operations, Finance, People, and Clinical leadership teams — async-by-default, with anchor sync hours during EST overlap\n\n - Communicate clearly and proactively across time zones, with strong written status updates\n\n - Escalate appropriately and exercise judgment in ambiguity\n\n \n\n\nQUALIFICATIONS\n\n\nREQUIRED\n\n - 3+ years in business operations, operations, consulting, finance operations, or a similar generalist role\n\n - Demonstrated ability to work full-time US Eastern Time hours (approx. 9 PM – 6 AM Manila time, including DST shifts)\n\n - Hands-on experience with modern business systems (e.g., Ramp/Bill.com http://Bill.com, Rippling or similar HRIS, QuickBooks exposure a plus)\n\n - Demonstrated AI fluency — must be able to show actual work product (Claude Projects, automations, prompt engineering, agent workflows, or similar). Curiosity is not enough; we want to see what you've built.\n\n - Excellent written English and async communication skills\n\n - Strong organizational judgment — able to prioritize, own, and finish work without close supervision\n\n \n\n\nPREFERRED\n\n - Experience supporting US-based healthcare, multi-site, or services organizations\n\n - Experience supporting new site openings, M&A integration, or market expansion\n\n - Experience in a startup or high-growth environment\n\n - Exposure to financial operations (AP, reconciliation, expense management)\n\n - Experience building dashboards or operational reporting\n\nIf you don't meet every preferred qualification, we still encourage you to apply.\n\n \n\n\nIDEAL CANDIDATE\n\nYou are a systems-minded operator who thrives in fast-moving, ambiguous environments. You are a builder at heart — comfortable owning cross-functional projects end-to-end, keeping operational data trustworthy, and turning messy processes into clean, documented systems. You balance meticulous execution with genuine creativity about how AI can multiply your output, and you're energized by the idea that the automations you build become permanent infrastructure for a growing organization. You are motivated by an opportunity to be an early, high-leverage operational hire at a mission-driven company transforming autism care across multiple states.\n\n \n\n\nWHY ANNA?\n\nAt ANNA, we are working to transform autism care by combining rigorous clinical training, compassionate family-centered practice, and neurodiversity-affirming approaches. Our Naturalistic Developmental Behavioral Intervention (NDBI) model supports each child's strengths through play-based, developmentally informed care.\n\nAs our Business Operations Specialist, you'll build the operational infrastructure that lets our clinical teams focus on what matters most — delivering exceptional care to children and families.\n\nYou can learn more about us here: https://annaautismcare.com/about-us/\n\n\n\nLocation: Remote, Philippines-based, full-time US Eastern hours.\n\nANNA Autism Care | Business Operations Specialist\n\n\n\nANNA is an equal opportunity employer. We're committed to creating a diverse, inclusive, and supportive workplace. All qualified applicants receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, national origin, age, disability, religion, sex (including pregnancy, sexual orientation, and gender identity), or any other characteristic protected by law. If you're passionate about our mission but don't meet every qualification listed, we still encourage you to apply. Your unique perspective might be exactly what we need.\"","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":"$24K – $36K","scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":"$24K - $36K","compensationTiers":[{"id":"bcc85dd8-1fa8-427b-bb7e-fef991fec5a9","tierSummary":"$24K – $36K","title":null,"additionalInformation":null,"components":[{"id":"7261d3e8-2c85-4b7a-9df5-fd0058a3f88e","summary":"$24K – $36K","compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":24000,"maxValue":36000}]}],"summaryComponents":[{"compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":24000,"maxValue":36000}]}},{"id":"40a4287a-3a32-4606-8e83-43c1425ea5e1","title":"Senior Talent Acquisition Specialist","department":"Support Team","team":"Operations","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"Remote - Canada","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":true,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-07-29T16:11:11.159+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Remote","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressCountry":"Canada"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/annaautismcare/40a4287a-3a32-4606-8e83-43c1425ea5e1","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/annaautismcare/40a4287a-3a32-4606-8e83-43c1425ea5e1/application","descriptionHtml":"<p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>ANNA Autism Care</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Senior Talent Acquisition Specialist</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Remote (Canada) | Full-time, US Eastern Hours</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">$90,000–$110,000 CAD (approximately $65,000–$80,000 USD) — top-of-market compensation for exceptional execution</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><h1><strong>About ANNA</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">ANNA (Allied Network for Neurodevelopmental Advancement) is a high-growth, high-impact healthcare startup focused on creating a future where every autistic child has access to joyful, evidence-based, and neuroaffirming care. We provide center-based ABA services to young autistic children (under the age of 6) and their families using a neurodiversity-affirming, Naturalistic Developmental Behavioral Intervention (NDBI) approach, with 6 centers and growing across Massachusetts and Missouri.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are an AI-native organization that operates at high velocity — AI is embedded in how we build our clinical systems, run our operations, and yes, how we hire. We're looking for a passionate, experienced recruiter to help us build the team behind our growth.</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><h1><strong>Position Overview</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">The Senior Talent Acquisition Specialist owns full-cycle recruiting across ANNA's three hiring lanes: BCBAs (Clinical Supervisors), Clinical Directors, and Corporate/Support roles (operations, finance, people, and engineering support functions). Reporting to the Director of People Operations, this is a hands-on, high-throughput role — you will source candidates directly, run structured phone screens, coordinate multi-round interview loops, build and maintain scorecards and hiring documentation, extend and negotiate offers, and own the operational backbone of ANNA's recruiting function, including SOPs, ATS hygiene, and pipeline reporting.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This role is high-velocity and operationally intensive by design. On any given week you may be running a dozen active screens, keeping multiple interview loops moving across time zones, administering a take-home case study for a corporate candidate, negotiating a BCBA offer, and updating an SOP — all while your sourcing pipelines keep filling. The volume is real and the bar for execution is high: candidates never sit waiting, interviewers always have their materials, and nothing falls through the cracks. If you're energized by throughput and precision at the same time, this is your role.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">ANNA runs a structured, artifact-driven hiring process built for speed: every role has a defined document suite, every interviewer works from behaviorally anchored scorecards, and AI tooling (Claude) is embedded in how we build and operate hiring infrastructure. Clinical hiring (BCBAs, Clinical Directors) runs on screens, structured interviews, and reference depth; corporate/support hiring adds paid take-home case studies that you'll administer end to end. You'll operate inside that system, improve it, and keep it moving at startup velocity as we scale across states.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Success is measured by time-to-fill on clinical and corporate roles, sourced-candidate pipeline volume and quality, offer acceptance rates, hiring manager and candidate experience, and the completeness and currency of recruiting operations infrastructure.</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><h1><strong>Compensation &amp; Engagement</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Base Salary</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">$90,000–$110,000 CAD (approximately $65,000–$80,000 USD) — top-of-market compensation for exceptional execution</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Time Off</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Flexible PTO</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Engagement Structure</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Full-time via Canadian Contractor of Record; no additional benefits provided</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Work Arrangement</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Fully remote from Canada; core working hours aligned to US Eastern Time</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><h1><strong>What You’ll Do</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Sourcing &amp; Pipeline Development</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">• Own proactive sourcing for BCBA and Clinical Director searches — direct outreach via LinkedIn Recruiter, BACB directories, ABA-specific job boards, and referral cultivation — in markets where licensed clinical talent is scarce and competitive</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">• Build and maintain evergreen pipelines for BCBAs in Massachusetts and Missouri, including pre-qualified passive candidates ahead of center openings</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">• Source and screen for corporate/support roles across operations, finance, and people functions, including US-based and Philippines-based positions</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">• Maintain sourcing performance data by channel (response rates, screen conversion, source-of-hire) and shift spend and effort toward what's working</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">• Write and continuously test outreach messaging that reflects ANNA's neurodiversity-affirming model and converts passive clinical talent</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Screening &amp; Interview Operations</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">• Conduct structured phone screens using ANNA's scorecard system, delivering calibrated 1–5 ratings with behavioral evidence — not gut reads</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">• Own end-to-end interview coordination: scheduling multi-interviewer loops across time zones, distributing scorecards and candidate materials to interviewers ahead of each round, and keeping every loop moving without candidate wait time</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">• Administer take-home case studies for corporate/support roles end to end — distribution, candidate questions, submission tracking, and candidate payment logistics (BCBA and Clinical Director processes do not include take-homes)</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">• Draft and maintain role scorecards, phone screen guides, and interview materials in partnership with hiring managers, following ANNA's established document standards</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">• Enforce process integrity: independent evaluator reads collected before interviewers compare notes, scorecards completed within SLA, debriefs scheduled promptly</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">• Manage all candidate communication — timely updates, rejections handled with care, and a candidate experience consistent with ANNA's brand</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Offers &amp; Closing</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">• Extend offers and lead negotiation within approved comp bands, partnering with the Director of People Operations and hiring managers on exceptions</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">• Manage the offer-to-start pipeline: background checks, credential verification (BCBA certification, licensure), COR/EOR onboarding handoffs, and start-date coordination with People Operations</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">• Track and improve offer acceptance rates, including structured loss-reason capture on declined offers</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Recruiting Operations &amp; Infrastructure</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">• Own Ashby (ATS) administration: pipeline stages, automations, scorecard templates, reporting dashboards, and data hygiene</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">• Build and maintain recruiting SOPs — sourcing playbooks by role type, screen-to-offer process documentation, interview loop templates, and onboarding handoff checklists — so the function runs consistently and can scale</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">• Produce weekly pipeline reporting for leadership: reqs by stage, aging, conversion rates, and forecast-to-fill against hiring plan</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">• Use AI tooling (Claude) as a working part of the job — drafting materials, structuring evaluation notes, building process documentation — consistent with how ANNA operates internally</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><h1><strong>Qualifications</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Required</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">• 5+ years of full-cycle recruiting experience, including significant in-house experience (not solely agency)</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">• Demonstrated success recruiting licensed or credentialed healthcare clinicians in competitive talent markets</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">• Proven direct-sourcing capability — you build pipelines yourself rather than waiting on inbound or relying on agencies</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">• Experience extending and negotiating offers, including navigating comp conversations with clinical candidates</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">• Strong recruiting operations skills: ATS administration, structured interview processes, SOP creation, and pipeline reporting</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">• Demonstrated AI fluency through real work product — you actively use AI tools in your recruiting workflow today and can show how</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">• Ability to work core US Eastern hours</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Preferred</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">• Experience recruiting BCBAs, ABA clinicians, or behavioral health professionals specifically</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">• Experience with Ashby or comparable modern ATS platforms</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">• Experience recruiting for multi-state or multi-site healthcare organizations</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">• Experience supporting international hiring (e.g., Philippines-based roles) and COR/EOR arrangements</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">• Experience in a startup or high-growth environment where you built recruiting infrastructure, not just operated it</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>If you don't meet every preferred qualification, we still encourage you to apply.</em></p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><h1><strong>Ideal Candidate</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You are a mission-driven recruiter who thrives in high-growth healthcare environments and genuinely enjoys operating at pace. You are a builder-operator who is equally comfortable cold-sourcing a BCBA in a tight market, running a calibrated screen, negotiating an offer, and writing the SOP that makes the whole process repeatable. High volume doesn't rattle you — it's where you're at your best, because your systems and discipline keep quality high even when throughput is heavy. You balance pipeline hustle with operational rigor and are energized by owning a function end-to-end rather than a slice of it. You are motivated by the opportunity to build the recruiting engine behind ANNA's multi-state expansion — putting exceptional clinicians and operators in front of children and families who need them.</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Why ANNA?</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At ANNA, we are working to transform autism care by combining rigorous clinical training, compassionate family-centered practice, and neurodiversity-affirming approaches. Our NDBI model supports each child’s strengths through play-based, developmentally informed care. This role is how we make sure that every time ANNA enters a new market, whether by opening a new center or absorbing an existing one, it comes online cleanly and runs well, so the operators and clinicians delivering that care can focus on kids and families.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Learn more about us: <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://annaautismcare.com/about-us/\">https://annaautismcare.com/about-us/</a></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Remote, Canada-based, full-time US Eastern hours.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">ANNA is an equal opportunity employer. We're committed to creating a diverse, inclusive, and supportive workplace. All qualified applicants receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, national origin, age, disability, religion, sex (including pregnancy, sexual orientation, and gender identity), or any other characteristic protected by law. If you're passionate about our mission but don't meet every qualification listed, we still encourage you to apply. Your unique perspective might be exactly what we need.\"</p>","descriptionPlain":"ANNA Autism Care\n\nSenior Talent Acquisition Specialist\n\nRemote (Canada) | Full-time, US Eastern Hours\n\n$90,000–$110,000 CAD (approximately $65,000–$80,000 USD) — top-of-market compensation for exceptional execution\n\n \n\n\nABOUT ANNA\n\nANNA (Allied Network for Neurodevelopmental Advancement) is a high-growth, high-impact healthcare startup focused on creating a future where every autistic child has access to joyful, evidence-based, and neuroaffirming care. We provide center-based ABA services to young autistic children (under the age of 6) and their families using a neurodiversity-affirming, Naturalistic Developmental Behavioral Intervention (NDBI) approach, with 6 centers and growing across Massachusetts and Missouri.\n\nWe are an AI-native organization that operates at high velocity — AI is embedded in how we build our clinical systems, run our operations, and yes, how we hire. We're looking for a passionate, experienced recruiter to help us build the team behind our growth.\n\n \n\n\nPOSITION OVERVIEW\n\nThe Senior Talent Acquisition Specialist owns full-cycle recruiting across ANNA's three hiring lanes: BCBAs (Clinical Supervisors), Clinical Directors, and Corporate/Support roles (operations, finance, people, and engineering support functions). Reporting to the Director of People Operations, this is a hands-on, high-throughput role — you will source candidates directly, run structured phone screens, coordinate multi-round interview loops, build and maintain scorecards and hiring documentation, extend and negotiate offers, and own the operational backbone of ANNA's recruiting function, including SOPs, ATS hygiene, and pipeline reporting.\n\nThis role is high-velocity and operationally intensive by design. On any given week you may be running a dozen active screens, keeping multiple interview loops moving across time zones, administering a take-home case study for a corporate candidate, negotiating a BCBA offer, and updating an SOP — all while your sourcing pipelines keep filling. The volume is real and the bar for execution is high: candidates never sit waiting, interviewers always have their materials, and nothing falls through the cracks. If you're energized by throughput and precision at the same time, this is your role.\n\nANNA runs a structured, artifact-driven hiring process built for speed: every role has a defined document suite, every interviewer works from behaviorally anchored scorecards, and AI tooling (Claude) is embedded in how we build and operate hiring infrastructure. Clinical hiring (BCBAs, Clinical Directors) runs on screens, structured interviews, and reference depth; corporate/support hiring adds paid take-home case studies that you'll administer end to end. You'll operate inside that system, improve it, and keep it moving at startup velocity as we scale across states.\n\nSuccess is measured by time-to-fill on clinical and corporate roles, sourced-candidate pipeline volume and quality, offer acceptance rates, hiring manager and candidate experience, and the completeness and currency of recruiting operations infrastructure.\n\n \n\n\nCOMPENSATION & ENGAGEMENT\n\nBase Salary\n\n$90,000–$110,000 CAD (approximately $65,000–$80,000 USD) — top-of-market compensation for exceptional execution\n\nTime Off\n\nFlexible PTO\n\nEngagement Structure\n\nFull-time via Canadian Contractor of Record; no additional benefits provided\n\nWork Arrangement\n\nFully remote from Canada; core working hours aligned to US Eastern Time\n\n \n\n\nWHAT YOU’LL DO\n\nSourcing & Pipeline Development\n\n• Own proactive sourcing for BCBA and Clinical Director searches — direct outreach via LinkedIn Recruiter, BACB directories, ABA-specific job boards, and referral cultivation — in markets where licensed clinical talent is scarce and competitive\n\n• Build and maintain evergreen pipelines for BCBAs in Massachusetts and Missouri, including pre-qualified passive candidates ahead of center openings\n\n• Source and screen for corporate/support roles across operations, finance, and people functions, including US-based and Philippines-based positions\n\n• Maintain sourcing performance data by channel (response rates, screen conversion, source-of-hire) and shift spend and effort toward what's working\n\n• Write and continuously test outreach messaging that reflects ANNA's neurodiversity-affirming model and converts passive clinical talent\n\nScreening & Interview Operations\n\n• Conduct structured phone screens using ANNA's scorecard system, delivering calibrated 1–5 ratings with behavioral evidence — not gut reads\n\n• Own end-to-end interview coordination: scheduling multi-interviewer loops across time zones, distributing scorecards and candidate materials to interviewers ahead of each round, and keeping every loop moving without candidate wait time\n\n• Administer take-home case studies for corporate/support roles end to end — distribution, candidate questions, submission tracking, and candidate payment logistics (BCBA and Clinical Director processes do not include take-homes)\n\n• Draft and maintain role scorecards, phone screen guides, and interview materials in partnership with hiring managers, following ANNA's established document standards\n\n• Enforce process integrity: independent evaluator reads collected before interviewers compare notes, scorecards completed within SLA, debriefs scheduled promptly\n\n• Manage all candidate communication — timely updates, rejections handled with care, and a candidate experience consistent with ANNA's brand\n\nOffers & Closing\n\n• Extend offers and lead negotiation within approved comp bands, partnering with the Director of People Operations and hiring managers on exceptions\n\n• Manage the offer-to-start pipeline: background checks, credential verification (BCBA certification, licensure), COR/EOR onboarding handoffs, and start-date coordination with People Operations\n\n• Track and improve offer acceptance rates, including structured loss-reason capture on declined offers\n\nRecruiting Operations & Infrastructure\n\n• Own Ashby (ATS) administration: pipeline stages, automations, scorecard templates, reporting dashboards, and data hygiene\n\n• Build and maintain recruiting SOPs — sourcing playbooks by role type, screen-to-offer process documentation, interview loop templates, and onboarding handoff checklists — so the function runs consistently and can scale\n\n• Produce weekly pipeline reporting for leadership: reqs by stage, aging, conversion rates, and forecast-to-fill against hiring plan\n\n• Use AI tooling (Claude) as a working part of the job — drafting materials, structuring evaluation notes, building process documentation — consistent with how ANNA operates internally\n\n \n\n\nQUALIFICATIONS\n\nRequired\n\n• 5+ years of full-cycle recruiting experience, including significant in-house experience (not solely agency)\n\n• Demonstrated success recruiting licensed or credentialed healthcare clinicians in competitive talent markets\n\n• Proven direct-sourcing capability — you build pipelines yourself rather than waiting on inbound or relying on agencies\n\n• Experience extending and negotiating offers, including navigating comp conversations with clinical candidates\n\n• Strong recruiting operations skills: ATS administration, structured interview processes, SOP creation, and pipeline reporting\n\n• Demonstrated AI fluency through real work product — you actively use AI tools in your recruiting workflow today and can show how\n\n• Ability to work core US Eastern hours\n\nPreferred\n\n• Experience recruiting BCBAs, ABA clinicians, or behavioral health professionals specifically\n\n• Experience with Ashby or comparable modern ATS platforms\n\n• Experience recruiting for multi-state or multi-site healthcare organizations\n\n• Experience supporting international hiring (e.g., Philippines-based roles) and COR/EOR arrangements\n\n• Experience in a startup or high-growth environment where you built recruiting infrastructure, not just operated it\n\nIf you don't meet every preferred qualification, we still encourage you to apply.\n\n \n\n\nIDEAL CANDIDATE\n\nYou are a mission-driven recruiter who thrives in high-growth healthcare environments and genuinely enjoys operating at pace. You are a builder-operator who is equally comfortable cold-sourcing a BCBA in a tight market, running a calibrated screen, negotiating an offer, and writing the SOP that makes the whole process repeatable. High volume doesn't rattle you — it's where you're at your best, because your systems and discipline keep quality high even when throughput is heavy. You balance pipeline hustle with operational rigor and are energized by owning a function end-to-end rather than a slice of it. You are motivated by the opportunity to build the recruiting engine behind ANNA's multi-state expansion — putting exceptional clinicians and operators in front of children and families who need them.\n\n \n\nWhy ANNA?\n\nAt ANNA, we are working to transform autism care by combining rigorous clinical training, compassionate family-centered practice, and neurodiversity-affirming approaches. Our NDBI model supports each child’s strengths through play-based, developmentally informed care. This role is how we make sure that every time ANNA enters a new market, whether by opening a new center or absorbing an existing one, it comes online cleanly and runs well, so the operators and clinicians delivering that care can focus on kids and families.\n\nLearn more about us: https://annaautismcare.com/about-us/\n\nRemote, Canada-based, full-time US Eastern hours.\n\nANNA is an equal opportunity employer. We're committed to creating a diverse, inclusive, and supportive workplace. All qualified applicants receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, national origin, age, disability, religion, sex (including pregnancy, sexual orientation, and gender identity), or any other characteristic protected by law. If you're passionate about our mission but don't meet every qualification listed, we still encourage you to apply. Your unique perspective might be exactly what we need.\"","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":"CA$90K – CA$110K","scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":"CA$90K - CA$110K","compensationTiers":[{"id":"ca9225b2-5ea9-46fe-b885-2b57fd747fb4","tierSummary":"CA$90K – CA$110K","title":null,"additionalInformation":null,"components":[{"id":"6779d41b-f495-4dbb-9114-e00af78dc28c","summary":"CA$90K – CA$110K","compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"CAD","minValue":90000,"maxValue":110000}]}],"summaryComponents":[{"compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"CAD","minValue":90000,"maxValue":110000}]}},{"id":"32fc4acb-a999-4709-8895-de90ecfaa88f","title":"Clinical Director ","department":"Clinical","team":"Clinical Directors","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"Andover","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-07-23T12:46:38.809+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":false,"workplaceType":"OnSite","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"Massachusetts","addressCountry":"United States"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/annaautismcare/32fc4acb-a999-4709-8895-de90ecfaa88f","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/annaautismcare/32fc4acb-a999-4709-8895-de90ecfaa88f/application","descriptionHtml":"<p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Clinical Director (Center-Based) | $115K-$125K Base</strong><br /><strong>Full-Time | No Weekends | No Travel</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Are you ready to lead a team where every day means real progress for a child? Where a BCBA helps a toddler communicate for the first time, or a Behavior Therapist turns a tough Tuesday into a breakthrough? That's what leading a center at ANNA feels like.<br /><br /><strong>ANNA (Allied Network for Neurodevelopmental Advancement) is where compassion meets evidence, and every child's strength shines. </strong>We provide neurodiversity-affirming, play-based therapy to autistic children under 6 across Massachusetts, using NDBI (Naturalistic Developmental Behavioral Intervention) — following each child's lead, building on their strengths, in the context of real play and real life. It's joyful, purposeful work, and as Clinical Director, you're the one who makes sure your whole team can do it well, every day.<br /><br /><strong>Our values:</strong> Excellent Care (#wholehearted). Kindness (#platinum). Inclusion (#IDIC). Teamwork (#together). Growth (#rainforest).</p><h2><br /><strong>Position Overview</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Reports To: </strong><em>Market Executive Director</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a 100% on-site, center-based role.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">The Clinical Director is the on-the-ground leader of one of ANNA's centers — effectively the CEO of the clinic. You'll own the clinical excellence, day-to-day operations, and team culture of your center, leading a group of BCBAs and Behavior Therapists (BTs) who deliver NDBI-based care to children ages 18 months to 6 years.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a role that blends deep clinical leadership with substantial operational ownership — the job is at least as much about running the clinic as it is about clinical supervision. You'll be the direct people manager for your BCBAs (and a level-two manager for BTs), owning their supervision, development, and performance, while also managing your center's budget, staffing, scheduling, and utilization.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Enjoy a stable Monday–Friday schedule — no nights, weekends, or travel required.</p><h2><br /><strong>Compensation &amp; Benefits</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Base Salary</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">$115,000–$125,000 annually</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Bonus Potential</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Annual bonus of up to $3,000 tied to Quality of Care </p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">A monthly bonus tied to your clinic's financial sustainability (client growth while ramping, then team utilization once ramped). </p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Both are metrics-based and not guaranteed compensation.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Schedule</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Monday–Friday, 8:00 AM–4:30 PM — no nights, weekends, or travel</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Benefits</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Comprehensive health, dental, and vision insurance</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">401(k) with company match</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Separate paid Sick time (40 hours/year)</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Vacation time (80–140 hours/year, growing with tenure)</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Professional Development</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Annual stipend for CEUs and conference attendance, with ongoing supervision and training</p></li></ul><h2><br /><strong>What You'll Do</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em><strong>Clinical Leadership &amp; Supervision</strong></em></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Own clinical quality of your center by monitoring client progress, Behavior Therapist treatment fidelity, BCBA implementation fidelity, and other key clinical quality indicators to ensure effective, consistent, and evidence-based care</p></li></ul><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Provide individual and group supervision to BCBAs and Behavior Therapists, ensuring high-quality service delivery and adherence to our neurodiversity-affirming, NDBI methodology</p></li></ul><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Supervise BCBAs as they conduct assessments, build intervention plans, and deliver high-quality parent coaching</p></li></ul><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Monitor clinical documentation and ensure compliance with legal and ethical guidelines</p></li></ul><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Coach and develop your clinical team, helping BCBAs and BTs grow into the next level of their careers</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em><strong>Run Your Clinic Like a CEO</strong></em></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Own your center's performance across growth, utilization, quality of care, staff and caregiver experience, and team engagement — the full picture of what makes a clinic thrive</p></li></ul><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Own the day-to-day operations of your center: staffing, scheduling, supply ordering, facilities, and budget</p></li></ul><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Manage utilization across your team — a key driver of both BT retention and your center's financial health — and coach BCBAs whose utilization falls below expectations</p></li></ul><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Partner with centralized Talent Acquisition, HR, and Finance teams to keep hiring, employee relations, and clinic finances running smoothly, while owning the outcomes for your center</p></li></ul><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Create a safe, clean, welcoming space for the children and families we serve</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em><strong>People Management</strong></em></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Serve as the direct people manager for your BCBAs and a level-two manager for BTs, including performance management</p></li></ul><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Lead hiring and onboarding for your center in partnership with Talent Acquisition</p></li></ul><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Foster a collaborative, supportive, fun work environment that keeps your team engaged and reduces turnover</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em><strong>Collaborate with Leadership</strong></em></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Work closely with ANNA's clinical and operational leadership to assess staffing and training needs and support team development initiatives</p></li></ul><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Participate in individual and group supervision with clinical leadership</p></li></ul><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Communicate effectively and proactively with your clinical team and the families we serve</p></li></ul><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Guide the development and revision of ANNA's clinical policies and procedures, ensuring alignment between clinical best practices and operational decisions</p></li></ul><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Participate in clinical development and research activities when available — for example, program development, pilots of new assessment or treatment tools, case presentations, and conference or research collaborations</p></li></ul><h2><br /><strong>Your Growth Path at ANNA</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Growth here is real and named. Clinical Directors who consistently perform at the highest level — across clinical quality, operational execution, and team leadership — can grow into a Senior Clinical Director, a role reserved for CDs who mentor and model for other clinic leaders across ANNA. Anna is growing, both within and outside Massachusetts. Additional opportunities for growth are available to exceptional Clinical Directors looking for growth beyond the clinic environment.</p><h2><br /><strong>Qualifications</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em><strong>Required</strong></em></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">10+ years of experience in ABA, including 5+ years of post-credential experience providing, supervising, or administering ABA services to children with autism spectrum disorder as a credentialed BCBA, with an active Massachusetts LABA (Licensed Applied Behavior Analyst) license — or equivalent graduate-level behavior analyst credential — in good standing, maintained throughout employment</p></li></ul><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Master's-level clinician; Ph.D. preferred</p></li></ul><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience with clinical leadership and supervision of BCBAs and/or Behavior Therapists</p></li></ul><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Extensive experience working with children under the age of 6</p></li></ul><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Commitment to a neurodiversity-affirming approach to clinical services</p></li></ul><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Comfort owning operational responsibilities such as budgeting, staffing, scheduling, and utilization management — this role is as much operational as it is clinical</p></li></ul><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience with insurance-based services and knowledge of insurance billing requirements</p></li></ul><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong communication and interpersonal skills</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em><strong>Preferred</strong></em></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience with Naturalistic Developmental Behavioral Interventions (e.g., ESDM, PRT, JASPER)</p></li></ul><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Prior experience owning the full operational performance of a center, unit, or department (budget, staffing, KPIs)</p></li></ul><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">In-depth knowledge of behavioral assessment and intervention</p></li></ul><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Proficiency with Microsoft Office Suite and online file storage systems</p></li></ul><h2><br /><strong>Ideal Candidate</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You are a clinician-leader who is equally comfortable running a supervision session and running a P&amp;L. You think of your center as your own business — you take ownership of its clinical quality, its financial health, and its team culture. You know that no two clinical director roles look exactly alike, and you're energized by the chance to define what great looks like at ANNA.</p><h2><br /><strong>Why ANNA?</strong></h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Competitive Salary &amp; Benefits — $115,000–$125,000 base, plus an annual bonus of up to $3,000 (Quality of Care) and a monthly bonus tied to clinic performance, comprehensive health, dental, and vision insurance, and 401(k) with company match</p></li></ul><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Work-Life Balance — a full-time Monday–Friday schedule with no evenings, weekends, or travel</p></li></ul><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Clinical Excellence — ANNA is a clinician-owned, mission-driven organization that invests in delivering the best possible services to our clients and families</p></li></ul><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Clinical Support — regular individual and group supervision from our clinical leadership team</p></li></ul><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Professional Development — an annual stipend for CEUs and conference attendance, ongoing training, and a track record of promoting clinical team members into leadership roles</p></li></ul><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Work Culture — quarterly team outings, frequent celebrations, and a genuinely fun, supportive team environment</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><br /><strong>Location: </strong><em>ANNA center locations (Massachusetts) — full-time, on-site</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Pay:</strong> $115,000.00 - $125,000.00 per year</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Work Location:</strong> In person</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">ANNA is an equal opportunity employer. We're committed to creating a diverse, inclusive, and supportive workplace. All qualified applicants receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, national origin, age, disability, religion, sex (including pregnancy, sexual orientation, and gender identity), or any other characteristic protected by law. If you're passionate about our mission but don't meet every qualification listed, we still encourage you to apply. Your unique perspective might be exactly what we need.\"</p>","descriptionPlain":"Clinical Director (Center-Based) | $115K-$125K Base\nFull-Time | No Weekends | No Travel\n\nAre you ready to lead a team where every day means real progress for a child? Where a BCBA helps a toddler communicate for the first time, or a Behavior Therapist turns a tough Tuesday into a breakthrough? That's what leading a center at ANNA feels like.\n\nANNA (Allied Network for Neurodevelopmental Advancement) is where compassion meets evidence, and every child's strength shines. We provide neurodiversity-affirming, play-based therapy to autistic children under 6 across Massachusetts, using NDBI (Naturalistic Developmental Behavioral Intervention) — following each child's lead, building on their strengths, in the context of real play and real life. It's joyful, purposeful work, and as Clinical Director, you're the one who makes sure your whole team can do it well, every day.\n\nOur values: Excellent Care (#wholehearted). Kindness (#platinum). Inclusion (#IDIC). Teamwork (#together). Growth (#rainforest).\n\n\n\nPOSITION OVERVIEW\n\nReports To: Market Executive Director\n\nThis is a 100% on-site, center-based role.\n\nThe Clinical Director is the on-the-ground leader of one of ANNA's centers — effectively the CEO of the clinic. You'll own the clinical excellence, day-to-day operations, and team culture of your center, leading a group of BCBAs and Behavior Therapists (BTs) who deliver NDBI-based care to children ages 18 months to 6 years.\n\nThis is a role that blends deep clinical leadership with substantial operational ownership — the job is at least as much about running the clinic as it is about clinical supervision. You'll be the direct people manager for your BCBAs (and a level-two manager for BTs), owning their supervision, development, and performance, while also managing your center's budget, staffing, scheduling, and utilization.\n\nEnjoy a stable Monday–Friday schedule — no nights, weekends, or travel required.\n\n\n\nCOMPENSATION & BENEFITS\n\nBase Salary\n\n - $115,000–$125,000 annually\n\nBonus Potential\n\n - Annual bonus of up to $3,000 tied to Quality of Care \n\n - A monthly bonus tied to your clinic's financial sustainability (client growth while ramping, then team utilization once ramped). \n\n - Both are metrics-based and not guaranteed compensation.\n\nSchedule\n\n - Monday–Friday, 8:00 AM–4:30 PM — no nights, weekends, or travel\n\nBenefits\n\n - Comprehensive health, dental, and vision insurance\n\n - 401(k) with company match\n\n - Separate paid Sick time (40 hours/year)\n\n - Vacation time (80–140 hours/year, growing with tenure)\n\nProfessional Development\n\n - Annual stipend for CEUs and conference attendance, with ongoing supervision and training\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU'LL DO\n\nClinical Leadership & Supervision\n\n - Own clinical quality of your center by monitoring client progress, Behavior Therapist treatment fidelity, BCBA implementation fidelity, and other key clinical quality indicators to ensure effective, consistent, and evidence-based care\n\n - Provide individual and group supervision to BCBAs and Behavior Therapists, ensuring high-quality service delivery and adherence to our neurodiversity-affirming, NDBI methodology\n\n - Supervise BCBAs as they conduct assessments, build intervention plans, and deliver high-quality parent coaching\n\n - Monitor clinical documentation and ensure compliance with legal and ethical guidelines\n\n - Coach and develop your clinical team, helping BCBAs and BTs grow into the next level of their careers\n\nRun Your Clinic Like a CEO\n\n - Own your center's performance across growth, utilization, quality of care, staff and caregiver experience, and team engagement — the full picture of what makes a clinic thrive\n\n - Own the day-to-day operations of your center: staffing, scheduling, supply ordering, facilities, and budget\n\n - Manage utilization across your team — a key driver of both BT retention and your center's financial health — and coach BCBAs whose utilization falls below expectations\n\n - Partner with centralized Talent Acquisition, HR, and Finance teams to keep hiring, employee relations, and clinic finances running smoothly, while owning the outcomes for your center\n\n - Create a safe, clean, welcoming space for the children and families we serve\n\nPeople Management\n\n - Serve as the direct people manager for your BCBAs and a level-two manager for BTs, including performance management\n\n - Lead hiring and onboarding for your center in partnership with Talent Acquisition\n\n - Foster a collaborative, supportive, fun work environment that keeps your team engaged and reduces turnover\n\nCollaborate with Leadership\n\n - Work closely with ANNA's clinical and operational leadership to assess staffing and training needs and support team development initiatives\n\n - Participate in individual and group supervision with clinical leadership\n\n - Communicate effectively and proactively with your clinical team and the families we serve\n\n - Guide the development and revision of ANNA's clinical policies and procedures, ensuring alignment between clinical best practices and operational decisions\n\n - Participate in clinical development and research activities when available — for example, program development, pilots of new assessment or treatment tools, case presentations, and conference or research collaborations\n\n\n\nYOUR GROWTH PATH AT ANNA\n\nGrowth here is real and named. Clinical Directors who consistently perform at the highest level — across clinical quality, operational execution, and team leadership — can grow into a Senior Clinical Director, a role reserved for CDs who mentor and model for other clinic leaders across ANNA. Anna is growing, both within and outside Massachusetts. Additional opportunities for growth are available to exceptional Clinical Directors looking for growth beyond the clinic environment.\n\n\n\nQUALIFICATIONS\n\nRequired\n\n - 10+ years of experience in ABA, including 5+ years of post-credential experience providing, supervising, or administering ABA services to children with autism spectrum disorder as a credentialed BCBA, with an active Massachusetts LABA (Licensed Applied Behavior Analyst) license — or equivalent graduate-level behavior analyst credential — in good standing, maintained throughout employment\n\n - Master's-level clinician; Ph.D. preferred\n\n - Experience with clinical leadership and supervision of BCBAs and/or Behavior Therapists\n\n - Extensive experience working with children under the age of 6\n\n - Commitment to a neurodiversity-affirming approach to clinical services\n\n - Comfort owning operational responsibilities such as budgeting, staffing, scheduling, and utilization management — this role is as much operational as it is clinical\n\n - Experience with insurance-based services and knowledge of insurance billing requirements\n\n - Strong communication and interpersonal skills\n\nPreferred\n\n - Experience with Naturalistic Developmental Behavioral Interventions (e.g., ESDM, PRT, JASPER)\n\n - Prior experience owning the full operational performance of a center, unit, or department (budget, staffing, KPIs)\n\n - In-depth knowledge of behavioral assessment and intervention\n\n - Proficiency with Microsoft Office Suite and online file storage systems\n\n\n\nIDEAL CANDIDATE\n\nYou are a clinician-leader who is equally comfortable running a supervision session and running a P&L. You think of your center as your own business — you take ownership of its clinical quality, its financial health, and its team culture. You know that no two clinical director roles look exactly alike, and you're energized by the chance to define what great looks like at ANNA.\n\n\n\nWHY ANNA?\n\n - Competitive Salary & Benefits — $115,000–$125,000 base, plus an annual bonus of up to $3,000 (Quality of Care) and a monthly bonus tied to clinic performance, comprehensive health, dental, and vision insurance, and 401(k) with company match\n\n - Work-Life Balance — a full-time Monday–Friday schedule with no evenings, weekends, or travel\n\n - Clinical Excellence — ANNA is a clinician-owned, mission-driven organization that invests in delivering the best possible services to our clients and families\n\n - Clinical Support — regular individual and group supervision from our clinical leadership team\n\n - Professional Development — an annual stipend for CEUs and conference attendance, ongoing training, and a track record of promoting clinical team members into leadership roles\n\n - Work Culture — quarterly team outings, frequent celebrations, and a genuinely fun, supportive team environment\n\n\nLocation: ANNA center locations (Massachusetts) — full-time, on-site\n\nPay: $115,000.00 - $125,000.00 per year\n\nWork Location: In person\n\n \n\nANNA is an equal opportunity employer. We're committed to creating a diverse, inclusive, and supportive workplace. All qualified applicants receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, national origin, age, disability, religion, sex (including pregnancy, sexual orientation, and gender identity), or any other characteristic protected by law. If you're passionate about our mission but don't meet every qualification listed, we still encourage you to apply. Your unique perspective might be exactly what we need.\"","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"35d61f62-36fe-4ccb-a35d-3148c39b90e8","title":"Board Certified Behavior Analyst (BCBA)","department":"Clinical","team":"Board Certified Behavior Analysts","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"Braintree","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-07-23T14:39:36.939+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":false,"workplaceType":"OnSite","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"Massachusetts","addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"Braintree"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/annaautismcare/35d61f62-36fe-4ccb-a35d-3148c39b90e8","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/annaautismcare/35d61f62-36fe-4ccb-a35d-3148c39b90e8/application","descriptionHtml":"<p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Board Certified Behavior Analyst (BCBA) — ABA Therapy</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>$85,000–$115,000/yr + Monthly Bonuses | Full-Time, 40 hrs/wk | Monday–Friday | No Evenings, Weekends, or Travel</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">ANNA Autism Care is seeking an experienced, mission-driven Board Certified Behavior Analyst (BCBA) to join our clinician-led team. We specialize in early intervention ABA therapy for Autistic children under age 6, using the neuroaffirming model, Naturalistic Developmental Behavioral Intervention, or NDBI (ESDM, PRT, JASPER).</p><h2><br /><strong>Why Join ANNA?</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em><strong>Competitive Salary &amp; Monthly Bonuses:</strong> </em>$85K–$115K base salary plus $30/hr for every billable hour over 100/month. Comprehensive health, dental, and vision insurance and 401(k) with company match.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em><strong>Work-Life Balance:</strong> </em>40-hour schedule, Monday–Friday. No travel, no evenings, no weekends.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em><strong>Manageable Caseloads:</strong> </em>Small, intentional caseloads so you can deliver high-quality clinical care — not just high volume, that adhere to evidence-based autism clinical care and genuine clinical growth.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em><strong>Clinician-Led, Mission-Driven Culture:</strong> </em>Every decision starts with what's best for the child. We stay current with research and hold ourselves to a high clinical standard with our NDBI approach.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em><strong>Strong Team Support: </strong></em>Regular individual and group supervision from experienced clinicians invested in your success.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em><strong>Professional Development: </strong></em>Annual CEU stipend, conference support, and clear pathways into clinical leadership.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em><strong>Purpose-Built Technology: </strong></em>Streamlined data collection and clinical management tools so you stay focused on clients, not paperwork.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em><strong>Team Culture:</strong> </em>Quarterly outings, milestone celebrations, and a team that genuinely collaborates and enjoys working together.</p><h2><br /><strong>Key Responsibilities:</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em><strong>Assessment &amp; Treatment Planning: </strong></em>Conduct comprehensive assessments and develop individualized, play-based treatment plans grounded in NDBI strategies for children ages 18 months to 6 years.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em><strong>Supervise &amp; Mentor:</strong> </em>Lead and mentor a team of 5 - 6 Behavior Therapists through weekly individual and group supervision, building confident and skilled practitioners.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em><strong>Family Partnership:</strong> </em>Implement a structured, curriculum-based parent training model which helps families learn NDBI strategies to practice and use at home.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em><strong>Data-Driven Decision Making: </strong></em>Monitor client progress through ongoing data collection and analysis, adjusting treatment plans proactively to drive meaningful milestones.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em><strong>Collaborative Care:</strong> </em>Work closely with fellow BCBAs and report to a Clinical Director who is invested in both your growth and the quality of care delivered.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em><strong>Clinical Growth:</strong> </em>Contribute to a culture of continuous learning by integrating current research and best practices in Autism and ABA therapy.</p><h2><br /><strong>Qualifications:</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em> <strong>BCBA certification (required).</strong></em></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience delivering ABA therapy to young, Autistic children, preferably under age 6.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">NDBI experience preferred (ESDM, PRT, and/or JASPER).</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Commitment to neurodiversity-affirming, evidence-based practice.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong interpersonal skills; ability to work both independently and collaboratively.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Compensation &amp; Benefits:</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Base salary: $85,000–$115,000/year</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Monthly bonus: $30/hr for every billable hour over 100/month</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Health, dental, and vision insurance</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">401(k) with company match</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Paid time off (vacation, sick, and holidays)</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Annual CEU stipend and professional development support</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Apply today and join ANNA Autism Care's mission to modernize early intervention ABA care to a higher standard.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">ANNA is an equal opportunity employer. We're committed to creating a diverse, inclusive, and supportive workplace. All qualified applicants receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, national origin, age, disability, religion, sex (including pregnancy, sexual orientation, and gender identity), or any other characteristic protected by law. If you're passionate about our mission but don't meet every qualification listed, we still encourage you to apply. Your unique perspective might be exactly what we need.\"</p>","descriptionPlain":"Board Certified Behavior Analyst (BCBA) — ABA Therapy\n\n$85,000–$115,000/yr + Monthly Bonuses | Full-Time, 40 hrs/wk | Monday–Friday | No Evenings, Weekends, or Travel\n\nANNA Autism Care is seeking an experienced, mission-driven Board Certified Behavior Analyst (BCBA) to join our clinician-led team. We specialize in early intervention ABA therapy for Autistic children under age 6, using the neuroaffirming model, Naturalistic Developmental Behavioral Intervention, or NDBI (ESDM, PRT, JASPER).\n\n\n\nWHY JOIN ANNA?\n\nCompetitive Salary & Monthly Bonuses: $85K–$115K base salary plus $30/hr for every billable hour over 100/month. Comprehensive health, dental, and vision insurance and 401(k) with company match.\n\nWork-Life Balance: 40-hour schedule, Monday–Friday. No travel, no evenings, no weekends.\n\nManageable Caseloads: Small, intentional caseloads so you can deliver high-quality clinical care — not just high volume, that adhere to evidence-based autism clinical care and genuine clinical growth.\n\nClinician-Led, Mission-Driven Culture: Every decision starts with what's best for the child. We stay current with research and hold ourselves to a high clinical standard with our NDBI approach.\n\nStrong Team Support: Regular individual and group supervision from experienced clinicians invested in your success.\n\nProfessional Development: Annual CEU stipend, conference support, and clear pathways into clinical leadership.\n\nPurpose-Built Technology: Streamlined data collection and clinical management tools so you stay focused on clients, not paperwork.\n\nTeam Culture: Quarterly outings, milestone celebrations, and a team that genuinely collaborates and enjoys working together.\n\n\n\nKEY RESPONSIBILITIES:\n\nAssessment & Treatment Planning: Conduct comprehensive assessments and develop individualized, play-based treatment plans grounded in NDBI strategies for children ages 18 months to 6 years.\n\nSupervise & Mentor: Lead and mentor a team of 5 - 6 Behavior Therapists through weekly individual and group supervision, building confident and skilled practitioners.\n\nFamily Partnership: Implement a structured, curriculum-based parent training model which helps families learn NDBI strategies to practice and use at home.\n\nData-Driven Decision Making: Monitor client progress through ongoing data collection and analysis, adjusting treatment plans proactively to drive meaningful milestones.\n\nCollaborative Care: Work closely with fellow BCBAs and report to a Clinical Director who is invested in both your growth and the quality of care delivered.\n\nClinical Growth: Contribute to a culture of continuous learning by integrating current research and best practices in Autism and ABA therapy.\n\n\n\nQUALIFICATIONS:\n\n BCBA certification (required).\n\n - Experience delivering ABA therapy to young, Autistic children, preferably under age 6.\n\n - NDBI experience preferred (ESDM, PRT, and/or JASPER).\n\n - Commitment to neurodiversity-affirming, evidence-based practice.\n\n - Strong interpersonal skills; ability to work both independently and collaboratively.\n\nCompensation & Benefits:\n\n - Base salary: $85,000–$115,000/year\n\n - Monthly bonus: $30/hr for every billable hour over 100/month\n\n - Health, dental, and vision insurance\n\n - 401(k) with company match\n\n - Paid time off (vacation, sick, and holidays)\n\n - Annual CEU stipend and professional development support\n\nApply today and join ANNA Autism Care's mission to modernize early intervention ABA care to a higher standard.\n\n\n\nANNA is an equal opportunity employer. We're committed to creating a diverse, inclusive, and supportive workplace. All qualified applicants receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, national origin, age, disability, religion, sex (including pregnancy, sexual orientation, and gender identity), or any other characteristic protected by law. If you're passionate about our mission but don't meet every qualification listed, we still encourage you to apply. Your unique perspective might be exactly what we need.\"","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"65378d4b-1dcd-48b3-8e15-fc0ec3c2a643","title":"People Operations Manager","department":"Support Team","team":"Operations","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"Remote - Canada","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-08-05T17:25:05.421+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Remote","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressCountry":"Canada"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/annaautismcare/65378d4b-1dcd-48b3-8e15-fc0ec3c2a643","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/annaautismcare/65378d4b-1dcd-48b3-8e15-fc0ec3c2a643/application","descriptionHtml":"<p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>ANNA Autism Care</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>People Operations Manager</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Remote (Canada) | Full-time, US Eastern Hours</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">CAD $95,000 – $135,000 (approximately $67,000–$96,000 USD) </p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><h1><strong>About ANNA</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">ANNA (Allied Network for Neurodevelopmental Advancement) is a mission-driven organization that provides ABA services to young autistic children (under the age of 6) and their families using a neurodiversity-affirming, Naturalistic Developmental Behavioral Intervention (NDBI) approach. We operate multiple centers across Massachusetts and Missouri (6 and growing!) and are looking for an exceptional People Operations builder to construct the people engine behind our growth.</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><h1><strong>Position Overview</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">The People Operations Manager will build and run the operational backbone of the employee experience across ANNA's US markets — onboarding workflows, payroll accuracy, multi-state compliance, employee relations, performance infrastructure, and workforce reporting.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a high-velocity build role with unusually broad ownership for a manager-level position. We are scaling across states, which means the compliance calendar, the policy library, the dashboards, and the ER processes largely remain to be created — you will create them, run them, and improve them simultaneously. This is deliberately a sleeves-rolled-up role: you'll be in the payroll run, the I-9 file, and the compliance tracker yourself, and that's by design. You'll own US employment infrastructure end to end from Canada: state registrations, payroll cycles in Rippling, credential and I-9 compliance for a frontline clinical workforce, and the leave-law and classification decisions that keep a multi-state healthcare employer clean.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">ANNA is an AI-native company, and we expect People Operations to be built that way — AI-assisted policy drafting, automated compliance monitoring, agentic onboarding workflows. You'll build people systems that most HR teams twice our size are still waiting on.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Strong performance in this seat has a defined growth path to Senior People Operations Manager.</em></p><h1><br /><strong>What This Role Is Really Like</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Builder-first. </strong>You'll create most systems from scratch. The satisfaction here is in standing things up.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>High-throughput. </strong>Payroll runs, compliance deadlines, ER cases, onboarding cohorts, and executive reporting all move on their own clocks. Strong operators find the rhythm; this role rewards them.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>AI-leveraged. </strong>The only way one person runs this scope is with AI doing the heavy lifting — and you'll build and improve those workflows yourself.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>High-agency. </strong>You'll spot the compliance gap or process failure before anyone assigns it to you — and fix it.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Precise at volume. </strong>I-9s, credential expirations, deduction accuracy — the work is recurring and consequential, and the standard is zero dropped balls.</p></li></ul><h1><br /><strong>Key Responsibilities &amp; Deliverables</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em><strong>Payroll &amp; HRIS Operations</strong></em></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Own end-to-end US payroll execution in Rippling across multiple states, including deductions, adjustments, and off-cycle runs, with a zero-defect standard</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Serve as system owner for the HRIS — configuration, workflow automation, data integrity, and integrations with ANNA's broader stack</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Manage benefits administration operations in partnership with brokers and carriers</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em><strong>Compliance &amp; Risk</strong></em></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Build and run the multi-state compliance calendar: state registrations, wage and hour requirements, leave laws, posting requirements, and healthcare-specific credentialing</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Own I-9 and work-authorization compliance and the credential-expiration monitoring system for clinical staff</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Maintain the policy library and employee handbook across states, using AI-assisted drafting and review</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em><strong>Onboarding &amp; Employee Lifecycle</strong></em></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Design and run onboarding workflows that get new clinical and corporate hires productive fast — measured in hours, with automation carrying the repetitive load</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Own offboarding, transfers, and lifecycle changes with clean documentation and system hygiene</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em><strong>Employee Relations &amp; Performance Infrastructure</strong></em></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Run ER casework end to end under US employment law — documentation, investigation support, performance improvement plans, and terminations — in partnership with leadership</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Build ANNA's performance management infrastructure: review cycles, calibration tooling, and the reporting behind them</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em><strong>Reporting &amp; AI-Native Systems</strong></em></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Build and maintain workforce dashboards leadership actually uses: headcount, retention, compliance status, payroll accuracy</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Continuously identify manual People processes and replace them with AI-powered or automated workflows you design yourself</p></li></ul><h1><br /><strong>Qualifications</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em><strong>Required</strong></em></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">4–6+ years in People Operations or HR operations, including time as an early People hire at a high-growth startup or scale-up</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Hands-on ownership of US employment infrastructure: multi-state payroll, state registrations, I-9 compliance, FLSA classification, and leave-law administration</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience personally running US ER cases end to end, including documentation and difficult conversations</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Demonstrated AI fluency through real work product — automated workflows, AI-assisted documentation systems, or reporting builds you created yourself</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ability to work US Eastern business hours</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Precision and follow-through at high volume</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em><strong>Preferred</strong></em></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Rippling administration experience</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience supporting a frontline, multi-site, or healthcare workforce (shift schedules, credential tracking, high-volume hiring)</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Background at an EOR, PEO, or payroll provider serving US clients</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience implementing or migrating an HRIS or payroll platform yourself</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>If you don't meet every preferred qualification, we still encourage you to apply.</em></p><h1><br /><strong>Ideal Candidate</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You are a precision-obsessed builder who thrives where systems remain to be created. You started somewhere structured — a payroll bureau, an EOR, people advisory — and it gave you zero-defect instincts; then you joined a scale-up as one of the first People hires and discovered you love standing things up at speed. You talk about your work in artifacts and numbers: the compliance calendar you built, the payroll migration you ran solo, the error rate you drove to zero. You use AI as a genuine work multiplier and have the workflows to prove it. You are energized by ownership well beyond a typical manager-level scope, and you're motivated by the chance to build the people engine of a mission-driven healthcare company from the ground up.<br /></p><h1><br /><strong>Compensation &amp; Benefits</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Base Compensation</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">CAD $95,000 – $135,000</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Engagement Structure</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Full-time engagement through a Contractor of Record in Canada</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Additional</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Paid time off and holidays; professional development and growth opportunities; supportive leadership and collaborative team culture</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1>Why Anna</h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At ANNA, we are working to transform autism care by combining rigorous clinical training, compassionate family-centered practice, and neurodiversity-affirming approaches. Our NDBI model supports each child's strengths through play-based, developmentally informed care. As People Operations Manager, you will build the systems that let our clinical teams focus entirely on children and families.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Learn more about us: <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://annaautismcare.com/about-us/\">https://annaautismcare.com/about-us/</a></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Remote, Canada-based, full-time US Eastern hours.</em><br /></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">ANNA is an equal opportunity employer. We're committed to creating a diverse, inclusive, and supportive workplace. All qualified applicants receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, national origin, age, disability, religion, sex (including pregnancy, sexual orientation, and gender identity), or any other characteristic protected by law. If you're passionate about our mission but don't meet every qualification listed, we still encourage you to apply. Your unique perspective might be exactly what we need.\"</p>","descriptionPlain":"ANNA Autism Care\n\nPeople Operations Manager\n\nRemote (Canada) | Full-time, US Eastern Hours\n\nCAD $95,000 – $135,000 (approximately $67,000–$96,000 USD) \n\n \n\n\nABOUT ANNA\n\nANNA (Allied Network for Neurodevelopmental Advancement) is a mission-driven organization that provides ABA services to young autistic children (under the age of 6) and their families using a neurodiversity-affirming, Naturalistic Developmental Behavioral Intervention (NDBI) approach. We operate multiple centers across Massachusetts and Missouri (6 and growing!) and are looking for an exceptional People Operations builder to construct the people engine behind our growth.\n\n \n\n\nPOSITION OVERVIEW\n\nThe People Operations Manager will build and run the operational backbone of the employee experience across ANNA's US markets — onboarding workflows, payroll accuracy, multi-state compliance, employee relations, performance infrastructure, and workforce reporting.\n\nThis is a high-velocity build role with unusually broad ownership for a manager-level position. We are scaling across states, which means the compliance calendar, the policy library, the dashboards, and the ER processes largely remain to be created — you will create them, run them, and improve them simultaneously. This is deliberately a sleeves-rolled-up role: you'll be in the payroll run, the I-9 file, and the compliance tracker yourself, and that's by design. You'll own US employment infrastructure end to end from Canada: state registrations, payroll cycles in Rippling, credential and I-9 compliance for a frontline clinical workforce, and the leave-law and classification decisions that keep a multi-state healthcare employer clean.\n\nANNA is an AI-native company, and we expect People Operations to be built that way — AI-assisted policy drafting, automated compliance monitoring, agentic onboarding workflows. You'll build people systems that most HR teams twice our size are still waiting on.\n\nStrong performance in this seat has a defined growth path to Senior People Operations Manager.\n\n\n\nWHAT THIS ROLE IS REALLY LIKE\n\n - Builder-first. You'll create most systems from scratch. The satisfaction here is in standing things up.\n\n - High-throughput. Payroll runs, compliance deadlines, ER cases, onboarding cohorts, and executive reporting all move on their own clocks. Strong operators find the rhythm; this role rewards them.\n\n - AI-leveraged. The only way one person runs this scope is with AI doing the heavy lifting — and you'll build and improve those workflows yourself.\n\n - High-agency. You'll spot the compliance gap or process failure before anyone assigns it to you — and fix it.\n\n - Precise at volume. I-9s, credential expirations, deduction accuracy — the work is recurring and consequential, and the standard is zero dropped balls.\n\n\n\nKEY RESPONSIBILITIES & DELIVERABLES\n\nPayroll & HRIS Operations\n\n - Own end-to-end US payroll execution in Rippling across multiple states, including deductions, adjustments, and off-cycle runs, with a zero-defect standard\n\n - Serve as system owner for the HRIS — configuration, workflow automation, data integrity, and integrations with ANNA's broader stack\n\n - Manage benefits administration operations in partnership with brokers and carriers\n\nCompliance & Risk\n\n - Build and run the multi-state compliance calendar: state registrations, wage and hour requirements, leave laws, posting requirements, and healthcare-specific credentialing\n\n - Own I-9 and work-authorization compliance and the credential-expiration monitoring system for clinical staff\n\n - Maintain the policy library and employee handbook across states, using AI-assisted drafting and review\n\nOnboarding & Employee Lifecycle\n\n - Design and run onboarding workflows that get new clinical and corporate hires productive fast — measured in hours, with automation carrying the repetitive load\n\n - Own offboarding, transfers, and lifecycle changes with clean documentation and system hygiene\n\nEmployee Relations & Performance Infrastructure\n\n - Run ER casework end to end under US employment law — documentation, investigation support, performance improvement plans, and terminations — in partnership with leadership\n\n - Build ANNA's performance management infrastructure: review cycles, calibration tooling, and the reporting behind them\n\nReporting & AI-Native Systems\n\n - Build and maintain workforce dashboards leadership actually uses: headcount, retention, compliance status, payroll accuracy\n\n - Continuously identify manual People processes and replace them with AI-powered or automated workflows you design yourself\n\n\n\nQUALIFICATIONS\n\nRequired\n\n - 4–6+ years in People Operations or HR operations, including time as an early People hire at a high-growth startup or scale-up\n\n - Hands-on ownership of US employment infrastructure: multi-state payroll, state registrations, I-9 compliance, FLSA classification, and leave-law administration\n\n - Experience personally running US ER cases end to end, including documentation and difficult conversations\n\n - Demonstrated AI fluency through real work product — automated workflows, AI-assisted documentation systems, or reporting builds you created yourself\n\n - Ability to work US Eastern business hours\n\n - Precision and follow-through at high volume\n\nPreferred\n\n - Rippling administration experience\n\n - Experience supporting a frontline, multi-site, or healthcare workforce (shift schedules, credential tracking, high-volume hiring)\n\n - Background at an EOR, PEO, or payroll provider serving US clients\n\n - Experience implementing or migrating an HRIS or payroll platform yourself\n\nIf you don't meet every preferred qualification, we still encourage you to apply.\n\n\n\nIDEAL CANDIDATE\n\nYou are a precision-obsessed builder who thrives where systems remain to be created. You started somewhere structured — a payroll bureau, an EOR, people advisory — and it gave you zero-defect instincts; then you joined a scale-up as one of the first People hires and discovered you love standing things up at speed. You talk about your work in artifacts and numbers: the compliance calendar you built, the payroll migration you ran solo, the error rate you drove to zero. You use AI as a genuine work multiplier and have the workflows to prove it. You are energized by ownership well beyond a typical manager-level scope, and you're motivated by the chance to build the people engine of a mission-driven healthcare company from the ground up.\n\n\n\n\nCOMPENSATION & BENEFITS\n\nBase Compensation\n\nCAD $95,000 – $135,000\n\nEngagement Structure\n\nFull-time engagement through a Contractor of Record in Canada\n\nAdditional\n\nPaid time off and holidays; professional development and growth opportunities; supportive leadership and collaborative team culture\n\n\n\n\nWHY ANNA\n\nAt ANNA, we are working to transform autism care by combining rigorous clinical training, compassionate family-centered practice, and neurodiversity-affirming approaches. Our NDBI model supports each child's strengths through play-based, developmentally informed care. As People Operations Manager, you will build the systems that let our clinical teams focus entirely on children and families.\n\nLearn more about us: https://annaautismcare.com/about-us/\n\nRemote, Canada-based, full-time US Eastern hours.\n\n\nANNA is an equal opportunity employer. We're committed to creating a diverse, inclusive, and supportive workplace. All qualified applicants receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, national origin, age, disability, religion, sex (including pregnancy, sexual orientation, and gender identity), or any other characteristic protected by law. If you're passionate about our mission but don't meet every qualification listed, we still encourage you to apply. Your unique perspective might be exactly what we need.\"","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"5c0801b9-cdc3-426b-89a2-04f28878b2c2","title":"Licensed Clinical Psychologist — Diagnostic Evaluations ","department":"Clinical","team":"Clinical","employmentType":"Contract","location":"Missouri","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-08-14T15:44:02.380+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Hybrid","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressCountry":"United States"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/annaautismcare/5c0801b9-cdc3-426b-89a2-04f28878b2c2","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/annaautismcare/5c0801b9-cdc3-426b-89a2-04f28878b2c2/application","descriptionHtml":"<p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>ANNA Autism Care</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Licensed Clinical Psychologist — Diagnostic Evaluations</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Remote or in person at ANNA's Missouri centers</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Independent Contractor (1099) | $150–$200 per hour</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><h1><strong>About ANNA</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">ANNA (Allied Network for Neurodevelopmental Advancement) is a mission-driven organization that provides ABA services to young autistic children (under the age of 6) and their families using a neurodiversity-affirming, Naturalistic Developmental Behavioral Intervention (NDBI) approach. We operate multiple centers across Massachusetts and Missouri and are looking for an experienced licensed psychologist to expand diagnostic access for Missouri families.</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><h1><strong>Position Overview</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">The Licensed Clinical Psychologist conducts diagnostic evaluations — delivered via telehealth or in person at ANNA's Missouri centers — for young children (under age 6) referred for suspected autism spectrum disorder across ANNA's Missouri market. This contractor role owns the full evaluation lifecycle: record review, caregiver interview, assessment administration, differential diagnosis, report writing, and family feedback sessions.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">The psychologist partners with ANNA's clinical and revenue cycle teams to ensure evaluations are timely, defensible to payors, and delivered with a neurodiversity-affirming, family-centered approach. Success is measured by evaluation timeliness, report quality and turnaround, family experience, and documentation that supports clean claims.</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><h1><strong>Ideal Candidate</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You are a skilled diagnostician who finds meaning in giving families clarity at one of the most consequential moments in their child's early life. You bring rigor to differential diagnosis, warmth to feedback conversations, and discipline to documentation and turnaround. You are energized by expanding diagnostic access for Missouri families and by helping shape an evaluation model — remote and in person — that is both clinically defensible and family-friendly.</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><h1><strong>Key Responsibilities</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em><strong>Diagnostic Evaluation Services</strong></em></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Conduct comprehensive diagnostic evaluations for children under 6 — via telehealth or in person at ANNA's Missouri centers — including developmental history, caregiver interview, standardized assessment, and behavioral observation</p></li></ul><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Select and administer a defensible battery matched to the delivery setting, from gold-standard in-person instruments (e.g., ADOS-2) to telehealth-adapted tools (e.g., TELE-ASD-PEDS, caregiver-report and adaptive measures)</p></li></ul><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Formulate differential diagnoses distinguishing ASD from language, developmental, and behavioral presentations</p></li></ul><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Produce comprehensive written reports meeting payor medical-necessity standards</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em><strong>Family Partnership &amp; Communication</strong></em></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Lead feedback sessions delivering diagnostic results with clarity, warmth, and neurodiversity-affirming framing</p></li></ul><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Prepare caregivers to participate effectively in the assessment process, including tele-administered sessions</p></li></ul><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Connect families to next steps, including ANNA's ABA services where clinically indicated</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em><strong>Documentation, Payor &amp; Quality</strong></em></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Maintain documentation that supports ANNA's clean claims standard and withstands payor audit</p></li></ul><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Complete payor credentialing (where applicable) and maintain active panel status</p></li></ul><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Adhere to Missouri telehealth regulations, informed consent requirements, and ANNA policies</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em><strong>Clinical Collaboration</strong></em></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Participate in monthly clinical syncs with ANNA clinical leadership</p></li></ul><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Respond to clinical and revenue cycle queries within 2 business days</p></li></ul><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Contribute to continuous improvement of ANNA's evaluation protocols</p></li></ul><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><h1><strong>Qualifications</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Required</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Doctorate in Clinical or School Psychology (PhD or PsyD)</p></li></ul><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Active, unrestricted Missouri psychologist license in good standing</p></li></ul><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">3+ years conducting pediatric diagnostic evaluations, including autism-specific assessment</p></li></ul><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Proficiency with gold-standard and telehealth-adapted instruments (ADOS-2, ADI-R, TELE-ASD-PEDS, Vineland-3, or equivalents)</p></li></ul><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ability to deliver evaluations via telehealth, in person at ANNA's Missouri centers, or both</p></li></ul><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Professional liability insurance; HIPAA-compliant remote work setup for telehealth delivery</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Preferred</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Active credentialing with MO HealthNet and major Missouri commercial payors</p></li></ul><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Deep experience with early childhood (under 6) presentations</p></li></ul><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Bilingual (Spanish a plus)</p></li></ul><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Comfort with technology-enabled clinical workflows, including AI-assisted documentation within PHI-compliant guardrails</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>If you don't meet every preferred qualification, we still encourage you to apply.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2><strong>Compensation &amp; Engagement</strong></h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Rate: $150–$200 per hour, based on experience, evaluation expertise, and payor credentialing status</p></li></ul><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Work remotely, in person at ANNA's Missouri centers, or a mix — with flexible scheduling built around your availability</p></li></ul><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Steady referral flow from ANNA's Missouri centers and community partners</p></li></ul><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Credentialing support provided by ANNA for psychologists joining without existing payor panels</p></li></ul><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Collaborative clinical community, including monthly clinical syncs with ANNA leadership</p></li></ul><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Professional development and growth opportunities</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Why ANNA?</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At ANNA, we are working to transform autism care by combining rigorous clinical training, compassionate family-centered practice, and neurodiversity-affirming approaches. Our NDBI model supports each child’s strengths through play-based, developmentally informed care. This role is how we make sure that every time ANNA enters a new market, whether by opening a new center or absorbing an existing one, it comes online cleanly and runs well, so the operators and clinicians delivering that care can focus on kids and families.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Learn more about us: <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://annaautismcare.com/about-us/\">https://annaautismcare.com/about-us/</a></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><br /></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">ANNA is an equal opportunity employer. We're committed to creating a diverse, inclusive, and supportive workplace. All qualified applicants receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, national origin, age, disability, religion, sex (including pregnancy, sexual orientation, and gender identity), or any other characteristic protected by law. If you're passionate about our mission but don't meet every qualification listed, we still encourage you to apply. Your unique perspective might be exactly what we need.\"</p>","descriptionPlain":"ANNA Autism Care\n\nLicensed Clinical Psychologist — Diagnostic Evaluations\n\nRemote or in person at ANNA's Missouri centers\n\nIndependent Contractor (1099) | $150–$200 per hour\n\n \n\n\nABOUT ANNA\n\nANNA (Allied Network for Neurodevelopmental Advancement) is a mission-driven organization that provides ABA services to young autistic children (under the age of 6) and their families using a neurodiversity-affirming, Naturalistic Developmental Behavioral Intervention (NDBI) approach. We operate multiple centers across Massachusetts and Missouri and are looking for an experienced licensed psychologist to expand diagnostic access for Missouri families.\n\n \n\n\nPOSITION OVERVIEW\n\nThe Licensed Clinical Psychologist conducts diagnostic evaluations — delivered via telehealth or in person at ANNA's Missouri centers — for young children (under age 6) referred for suspected autism spectrum disorder across ANNA's Missouri market. This contractor role owns the full evaluation lifecycle: record review, caregiver interview, assessment administration, differential diagnosis, report writing, and family feedback sessions.\n\nThe psychologist partners with ANNA's clinical and revenue cycle teams to ensure evaluations are timely, defensible to payors, and delivered with a neurodiversity-affirming, family-centered approach. Success is measured by evaluation timeliness, report quality and turnaround, family experience, and documentation that supports clean claims.\n\n \n\n\nIDEAL CANDIDATE\n\nYou are a skilled diagnostician who finds meaning in giving families clarity at one of the most consequential moments in their child's early life. You bring rigor to differential diagnosis, warmth to feedback conversations, and discipline to documentation and turnaround. You are energized by expanding diagnostic access for Missouri families and by helping shape an evaluation model — remote and in person — that is both clinically defensible and family-friendly.\n\n \n\n\nKEY RESPONSIBILITIES\n\nDiagnostic Evaluation Services\n\n - Conduct comprehensive diagnostic evaluations for children under 6 — via telehealth or in person at ANNA's Missouri centers — including developmental history, caregiver interview, standardized assessment, and behavioral observation\n\n - Select and administer a defensible battery matched to the delivery setting, from gold-standard in-person instruments (e.g., ADOS-2) to telehealth-adapted tools (e.g., TELE-ASD-PEDS, caregiver-report and adaptive measures)\n\n - Formulate differential diagnoses distinguishing ASD from language, developmental, and behavioral presentations\n\n - Produce comprehensive written reports meeting payor medical-necessity standards\n\nFamily Partnership & Communication\n\n - Lead feedback sessions delivering diagnostic results with clarity, warmth, and neurodiversity-affirming framing\n\n - Prepare caregivers to participate effectively in the assessment process, including tele-administered sessions\n\n - Connect families to next steps, including ANNA's ABA services where clinically indicated\n\nDocumentation, Payor & Quality\n\n - Maintain documentation that supports ANNA's clean claims standard and withstands payor audit\n\n - Complete payor credentialing (where applicable) and maintain active panel status\n\n - Adhere to Missouri telehealth regulations, informed consent requirements, and ANNA policies\n\nClinical Collaboration\n\n - Participate in monthly clinical syncs with ANNA clinical leadership\n\n - Respond to clinical and revenue cycle queries within 2 business days\n\n - Contribute to continuous improvement of ANNA's evaluation protocols\n\n \n\n\nQUALIFICATIONS\n\nRequired\n\n - Doctorate in Clinical or School Psychology (PhD or PsyD)\n\n - Active, unrestricted Missouri psychologist license in good standing\n\n - 3+ years conducting pediatric diagnostic evaluations, including autism-specific assessment\n\n - Proficiency with gold-standard and telehealth-adapted instruments (ADOS-2, ADI-R, TELE-ASD-PEDS, Vineland-3, or equivalents)\n\n - Ability to deliver evaluations via telehealth, in person at ANNA's Missouri centers, or both\n\n - Professional liability insurance; HIPAA-compliant remote work setup for telehealth delivery\n\nPreferred\n\n - Active credentialing with MO HealthNet and major Missouri commercial payors\n\n - Deep experience with early childhood (under 6) presentations\n\n - Bilingual (Spanish a plus)\n\n - Comfort with technology-enabled clinical workflows, including AI-assisted documentation within PHI-compliant guardrails\n\nIf you don't meet every preferred qualification, we still encourage you to apply.\n\n\n\n\nCOMPENSATION & ENGAGEMENT\n\n - Rate: $150–$200 per hour, based on experience, evaluation expertise, and payor credentialing status\n\n - Work remotely, in person at ANNA's Missouri centers, or a mix — with flexible scheduling built around your availability\n\n - Steady referral flow from ANNA's Missouri centers and community partners\n\n - Credentialing support provided by ANNA for psychologists joining without existing payor panels\n\n - Collaborative clinical community, including monthly clinical syncs with ANNA leadership\n\n - Professional development and growth opportunities\n\nWhy ANNA?\n\nAt ANNA, we are working to transform autism care by combining rigorous clinical training, compassionate family-centered practice, and neurodiversity-affirming approaches. Our NDBI model supports each child’s strengths through play-based, developmentally informed care. This role is how we make sure that every time ANNA enters a new market, whether by opening a new center or absorbing an existing one, it comes online cleanly and runs well, so the operators and clinicians delivering that care can focus on kids and families.\n\nLearn more about us: https://annaautismcare.com/about-us/\n\n\n\n\nANNA is an equal opportunity employer. We're committed to creating a diverse, inclusive, and supportive workplace. All qualified applicants receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, national origin, age, disability, religion, sex (including pregnancy, sexual orientation, and gender identity), or any other characteristic protected by law. If you're passionate about our mission but don't meet every qualification listed, we still encourage you to apply. Your unique perspective might be exactly what we need.\"","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}}],"apiVersion":"1"}